{"node_id":"NRS_484B_280_1a","law_refs":["NRS-484B-280-1a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"A driver of a motor vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"p2","text":"shall: Exercise due care","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"to avoid a collision with a pedestrian.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motor vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle, the definition that applies: 'every vehicle which is self-propelled but not operated upon rails', which 'does not include an electric bicycle or an electric scooter'; the run's reading classifies the classes under that id, so the aggregate is claimed whole and never expanded into class atoms. 'A driver of' names who controls the vehicle, no class: it is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (narrowing, observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["rel.contact","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a collision' is rel.contact: 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)'. Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: a near miss' does not apply: the collision itself is what the duty is to avoid, and the approach short of contact is read by the operationalization of 'due care', not by this atom. 'a pedestrian' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian: 'a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'; claimed whole and read for every road user of the scene other than ego."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"due care","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","drv.motion.at_rest"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: while the motor vehicle moves (drv.motion.at_rest under p.rest_speed_tolerance does not hold), a pedestrian whose centre it approaches within the time-to-collision horizon p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance) is a conflict the driver's care did not avoid; the projected distance enters the bound itself, so a nearer approach is a graver one. Care is a state of mind and the standard is the whole duty: the rule is a surrogate.","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a motor vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle). The duty is judged at every observation.","obligation":"At every observation, for every road user p of the scene other than ego that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian): either ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), or ego and p are not in contact (rel.contact) and it is not the case that their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) with a centre distance at that closest approach below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance). With no pedestrian in the scene the duty is met.","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p1","why":"'A driver' is read through the motor vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"p2","why":"'due care' is read only as the avoidance of contact and of a projected close approach to a pedestrian while the vehicle moves; lookout, warning and attention are read only through that outcome, and contact made while the vehicle is at rest is not read as a want of care.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle), drives along a roadway toward a pedestrian crossing in front of it; the centres are projected to approach within the horizon to a distance below the pedestrian clearance, and ego keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego drives past a pedestrian walking on the sidewalk well clear of the roadway; no projected approach falls below the clearance within the horizon and there is no contact."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego is a bicycle (ru.bicycle), which the motor vehicle aggregate does not include; it rides close past a pedestrian."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in permit, the projected approach stays above the clearance, but the source does not observe contact between bodies, so whether ego touches the pedestrian it passes is unknown.","masked":["rel.contact"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego drives along an empty road with no pedestrian anywhere in the scene: the duty binds ego alone and is met."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique (time-to-collision thresholds); proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_297_6_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-297-6"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"A pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"s2","text":"walking or otherwise traveling on a sidewalk","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s3","text":"who encounters an obstruction to his or her mobility on the sidewalk,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s4","text":"including, without limitation, a short section of the sidewalk that is missing or impassable,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s5","text":"may proceed","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s6","text":"with due care","role":"standard"},{"id":"s7","text":"on the immediately adjacent highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s8","text":"to move around such an obstruction.","role":"condition"},{"id":"s9","text":"Such a pedestrian:","role":"subject"},{"id":"s10","text":"(a) Must walk or otherwise travel as far to the side of the highway near the sidewalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s11","text":"as possible;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s12","text":"(b) May walk or otherwise travel on the highway in the direction he or she was walking or traveling on the sidewalk, regardless of the direction of traffic;","role":"exception"},{"id":"s13","text":"(c) May walk or otherwise travel in a lane provided for bicycles, electric bicycles or electric scooters","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s14","text":"if the area between the lane and the sidewalk is impassable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s15","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s16","text":"(d) Must return to the sidewalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"as soon as practicable.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrian' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian: 'a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'; claimed whole."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', which carries DEF-NRS-484A-240 ('that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies) is its walking on it, read at the earlier observation at which ego met the obstruction. 'Not a stand-in for: a crosswalk' does not apply: no crossing is read."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"st.obstruction is 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user', kinds including sidewalk_fixture, barrier, excavation, debris: an object in the pedestrian's way on the sidewalk. 'encounters' is ego at the obstruction while on the sidewalk: drv.position.near_region(ego, o) with the reach p.obstruction_reach, over the body-to-region distance of st.region_geometry, the anchor of the obstruction to ego. 'to his or her mobility' is read through ego's conduct at it (s8): it leaves the sidewalk there."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on s4): a short section of the sidewalk that is missing is no 'physical object' (st.obstruction), and the absence of a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk) is not a stretch a source records that a pedestrian meets. The example widens where the permission and the duties arise; dropping it would leave the rule unapplied where the law applies."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed' is ego's travel off the sidewalk onto the travelled part of the way: its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a region of kind st.travel_region, the abstract union of 'a lane ..., a bicycle lane or path, a roadway ..., a shoulder, or an intersection'; its exclusion of 'a sidewalk, a crosswalk' is the point: ego is off the sidewalk."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway","st.on_way","st.travel_region","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the immediately adjacent highway' is the same way as the sidewalk: the travel region ego occupies and the sidewalk it left both lie on one highway region (st.on_way, 'the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on'; st.highway, 'the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks'). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: nearness to a way' is respected: belonging is read through st.on_way, never a distance."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk","st.obstruction"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"'to move around such an obstruction' is a purpose, read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): since the last observation at which ego occupied the sidewalk while at that obstruction (drv.position.near_region), ego has occupied no sidewalk. 'such an obstruction' is the one s3 binds, re-bound with the same relations."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such a pedestrian' is the pedestrian of s1 who proceeds on the highway under the first sentence: the same binder, the same admitted aggregate."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s6","standard":"due care","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","drv.motion.at_rest","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.pedestrian"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: while the pedestrian moves on the highway (drv.motion.at_rest under p.rest_speed_tolerance does not hold), a member of traffic that is not a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not ru.pedestrian) whose centre it approaches within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance) is a conflict the pedestrian's care did not avoid; the projected distance enters the bound. Care is a state of mind: the rule is a surrogate.","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s12","why":"A permission to walk in either direction on the highway: no duty of this node turns on the direction of travel, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"ego is a pedestrian. At the judged observation ego occupies no sidewalk and occupies a travel region x (st.travel_region) lying on a highway h (st.on_way) on which a sidewalk s also lies; and, since the last observation at which ego occupied s while at an obstruction o (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), ego has occupied no sidewalk at any observation (a since operator). The case of a missing section of sidewalk is not carried (gap on s4).","obligation":"At the judged observation: ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), or for every road user u other than ego that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and not a pedestrian (ru.pedestrian), it is not the case that their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) with a centre distance at that closest approach below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance). With no such road user in the scene the duty is met.","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.obstruction_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s6","why":"'due care' is read only as the avoidance of a projected close approach to vehicular traffic while the pedestrian moves on the highway.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego walks along the sidewalk, reaches a barrier (st.obstruction) across it, steps onto the adjacent roadway of the same highway and walks into the path of an approaching car; their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the clearance while ego keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego steps onto the roadway only after the car has passed; no projected approach to any vehicle falls below the clearance."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego walks along the sidewalk past a mail drop box and never leaves the sidewalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks in the roadway beside the sidewalk with a car closing on it, but the source does not observe obstructions, so whether ego left the sidewalk at an obstruction is unknown.","masked":["st.obstruction"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego moves around a sidewalk excavation on the roadway with no other road user in the scene: the duty binds ego alone and is met."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique (time-to-collision thresholds); proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.obstruction_reach","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Reach within which a pedestrian counts as at an obstruction: a walking pedestrian's body width plus one step.","source":"pedestrian body ellipse and walking step length (HCM pedestrian space)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_interruption` | a stretch along a sidewalk where no walkable sidewalk exists (a section missing, removed, closed or broken up), carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so a pedestrian's arrival at it is read through st.region_geometry **Not a stand-in for:** an object standing on the sidewalk (st.obstruction) | general","nearest":["st.obstruction: 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user' (a missing section of sidewalk is no object, so the atom leaves out where the permission and the duties arise)","st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (the absence of a sidewalk region is not a stretch the source records that a pedestrian meets)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_297_6_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-297-6"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"A pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"s2","text":"walking or otherwise traveling on a sidewalk","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s3","text":"who encounters an obstruction to his or her mobility on the sidewalk,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s4","text":"including, without limitation, a short section of the sidewalk that is missing or impassable,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s5","text":"may proceed","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s6","text":"with due care","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s7","text":"on the immediately adjacent highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s8","text":"to move around such an obstruction.","role":"condition"},{"id":"s9","text":"Such a pedestrian:","role":"subject"},{"id":"s10","text":"(a) Must walk or otherwise travel as far to the side of the highway near the sidewalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s11","text":"as possible;","role":"standard"},{"id":"s12","text":"(b) May walk or otherwise travel on the highway in the direction he or she was walking or traveling on the sidewalk, regardless of the direction of traffic;","role":"exception"},{"id":"s13","text":"(c) May walk or otherwise travel in a lane provided for bicycles, electric bicycles or electric scooters","role":"exception"},{"id":"s14","text":"if the area between the lane and the sidewalk is impassable;","role":"standard"},{"id":"s15","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s16","text":"(d) Must return to the sidewalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s17","text":"as soon as practicable.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrian' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian: 'a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'; claimed whole."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', which carries DEF-NRS-484A-240 ('that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies) is its walking on it, read at the earlier observation at which ego met the obstruction. 'Not a stand-in for: a crosswalk' does not apply."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"st.obstruction is 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'; 'encounters' is ego at the obstruction while on the sidewalk: drv.position.near_region(ego, o) with p.obstruction_reach, over the body-to-region distance of st.region_geometry, the anchor of the obstruction to ego. 'to his or her mobility' is read through ego's conduct at it (s8)."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on s4): a missing section of sidewalk is no 'physical object' (st.obstruction), and the absence of a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk) is not a stretch a source records that a pedestrian meets."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed' is ego's travel off the sidewalk: its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a region of kind st.travel_region ('a lane ..., a bicycle lane or path, a roadway ..., a shoulder, or an intersection'), which excludes 'a sidewalk'."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway","st.on_way","st.travel_region","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the immediately adjacent highway' is the same way as the sidewalk: the travel region ego occupies and the sidewalk both lie on one highway region (st.on_way; st.highway 'including sidewalks and shoulders'); belonging is read through st.on_way, never a distance ('Not a stand-in for: nearness to a way')."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk","st.obstruction"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"A purpose read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): since the last observation at which ego occupied the sidewalk while at that obstruction, ego has occupied no sidewalk."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such a pedestrian' is the pedestrian of s1 proceeding under the first sentence: the same binder and aggregate."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["st.sidewalk","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"'as far to the side of the highway near the sidewalk' is ego's position across the way relative to the sidewalk: the ground distance from ego's body outline to the sidewalk region (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'), the sidewalk being the one ego left (s2, re-bound). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: occupancy' does not apply: ego is off the sidewalk."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.bicycle_lane_or_path"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a lane provided for bicycles, electric bicycles or electric scooters' is st.bicycle_lane_or_path, 'lane or separate path reserved for bicycles and the devices a jurisdiction groups with them'; ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies). The class words qualify the lane, not a road user the duty reads, so no aggregate is claimed."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s11","standard":"as possible","concepts":["st.region_geometry","prim.region_lateral_offset","st.obstruction"],"params":["p.pedestrian_edge_margin"],"convention":"Lateral position at the edge: the body-to-sidewalk distance (st.region_geometry) is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin, a step's width plus the shy distance a walker keeps from a curb; where an obstruction lies across ego's side toward the sidewalk (prim.region_lateral_offset of the obstruction of the same sign as the sidewalk's and of smaller magnitude), the nearest thing ego can keep to is that obstruction, and its body-to-obstruction distance is held to the same margin. The obstruction's own lateral reach moves the bound.","surrogate":false},{"span":"s14","standard":"impassable","concepts":["prim.region_lateral_offset","st.obstruction","drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.sidewalk"],"params":["p.obstruction_reach"],"convention":"An area is impassable on foot where a physical object blocks it: an obstruction lies laterally between ego and the sidewalk (prim.region_lateral_offset of the obstruction of the same sign as the sidewalk's and of smaller magnitude) and within p.obstruction_reach of ego (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry).","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s12","why":"A permission to walk in either direction on the highway: the duty to keep to the side near the sidewalk is the same in either direction, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_297_6_o1: ego is a pedestrian; at the judged observation ego occupies no sidewalk and occupies a travel region lying on a highway h on which a sidewalk s also lies, and since the last observation at which ego occupied s while at an obstruction (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), ego has occupied no sidewalk. Exception (c): not where ego occupies a bicycle lane or path (st.bicycle_lane_or_path) and an obstruction lies laterally between ego and s within p.obstruction_reach of ego.","obligation":"For the sidewalk s selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): the distance from ego's body to s (st.region_geometry) is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin, or an obstruction o lies laterally between ego and s (prim.region_lateral_offset of o of the same sign as that of s and of smaller magnitude) and the distance from ego's body to o is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin.","params":["p.pedestrian_edge_margin","p.obstruction_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s14","why":"'impassable' is read only through a physical object between the bicycle lane and the sidewalk; a strip impassable for other reasons (standing vehicles, a drop-off) is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks down the middle of the adjacent lane, well beyond the edge margin from both the sidewalk and the barrier."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks along the roadway hugging the barrier's outer side, within the edge margin of it, then of the sidewalk."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego stays on the sidewalk throughout."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks in the roadway after leaving the sidewalk at a barrier, but the source maps regions without outlines, so ego's distance to the sidewalk and to the barrier is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego walks in a bicycle lane beside a strip of excavation that lies between the lane and the sidewalk within the reach: exception (c) applies."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.pedestrian_edge_margin","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"Lateral body-to-edge distance within which a pedestrian walking on the highway counts as at the side next to the sidewalk or the obstruction: a step's width plus the shy distance a walker keeps from a curb or an object.","source":"pedestrian shy distance (HCM pedestrian facilities)"},{"name":"p.obstruction_reach","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Reach within which a pedestrian counts as at an obstruction: a walking pedestrian's body width plus one step.","source":"pedestrian body ellipse and walking step length (HCM pedestrian space)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_interruption` | a stretch along a sidewalk where no walkable sidewalk exists (a section missing, removed, closed or broken up), carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so a pedestrian's arrival at it is read through st.region_geometry **Not a stand-in for:** an object standing on the sidewalk (st.obstruction) | general","nearest":["st.obstruction: 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user' (a missing section of sidewalk is no object, so the atom leaves out where the duty arises)","st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (the absence of a sidewalk region is not a stretch the source records that a pedestrian meets)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_297_6_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-297-6"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"A pedestrian","role":"subject"},{"id":"s2","text":"walking or otherwise traveling on a sidewalk","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s3","text":"who encounters an obstruction to his or her mobility on the sidewalk,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s4","text":"including, without limitation, a short section of the sidewalk that is missing or impassable,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s5","text":"may proceed","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s6","text":"with due care","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s7","text":"on the immediately adjacent highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s8","text":"to move around such an obstruction.","role":"condition"},{"id":"s9","text":"Such a pedestrian:","role":"subject"},{"id":"s10","text":"(a) Must walk or otherwise travel as far to the side of the highway near the sidewalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s11","text":"as possible;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s12","text":"(b) May walk or otherwise travel on the highway in the direction he or she was walking or traveling on the sidewalk, regardless of the direction of traffic;","role":"exception"},{"id":"s13","text":"(c) May walk or otherwise travel in a lane provided for bicycles, electric bicycles or electric scooters","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s14","text":"if the area between the lane and the sidewalk is impassable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"s15","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s16","text":"(d) Must return to the sidewalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s17","text":"as soon as practicable.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrian' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian: 'a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'; claimed whole."},{"span":"s2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', carrying DEF-NRS-484A-240 ('intended for the use of pedestrians'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies), read at the earlier observation at which ego met the obstruction."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"st.obstruction is 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'; 'encounters' is ego at the obstruction while on the sidewalk: drv.position.near_region(ego, o) with p.obstruction_reach over st.region_geometry, the anchor of the obstruction to ego."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on s4): a missing section of sidewalk is no 'physical object' (st.obstruction), and the absence of a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk) is not a stretch a source records that a pedestrian meets."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed' is ego's travel off the sidewalk: its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a region of kind st.travel_region, which excludes 'a sidewalk'."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway","st.on_way","st.travel_region","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the immediately adjacent highway' is the same way as the sidewalk: the travel region ego occupies and the sidewalk both lie on one highway region (st.on_way); belonging is never read from a distance."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk","st.obstruction"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"A purpose read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): since the last observation at which ego occupied the sidewalk while at that obstruction, ego has occupied no sidewalk."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such a pedestrian' is the pedestrian of s1: the same binder and aggregate."},{"span":"s16","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'return to the sidewalk' is ego's footprint again overlapping (rel.occupies) a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk, 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line')."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s17","standard":"as soon as practicable","concepts":["drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.obstruction"],"params":["p.obstruction_reach","p.sidewalk_return_time"],"convention":"A return is practicable once the obstruction is behind the pedestrian: from the observation at which ego ceased to be at the obstruction (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach no longer holds; Term.sinceRise of its negation), ego is to be back on a sidewalk before p.sidewalk_return_time has elapsed, the walking time at a design walking speed to the next point where the sidewalk can be regained. The time elapsed since passing the obstruction enters the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s12","why":"A permission to walk in either direction on the highway: the duty to return to the sidewalk is the same in either direction, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_297_6_o1: ego is a pedestrian; at the judged observation ego occupies no sidewalk and occupies a travel region lying on a highway h on which a sidewalk s also lies, and since the last observation at which ego occupied s while at an obstruction o (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), ego has occupied no sidewalk.","obligation":"For the obstruction o selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego is at o (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), or the time since ego ceased to be at o (Term.sinceRise of not drv.position.near_region(ego, o)) is below p.sidewalk_return_time. Once ego occupies a sidewalk again the applicability no longer holds.","params":["p.obstruction_reach","p.sidewalk_return_time"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s17","why":"'as soon as practicable' is read as a return within a fixed time after the obstruction is behind the pedestrian; a sidewalk that stays blocked beyond the obstruction is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier, passes it on the roadway, and keeps walking on the roadway beside a free sidewalk long after the barrier is behind it."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier, passes it on the roadway and steps back onto the sidewalk shortly after the barrier is behind it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego stays on the sidewalk throughout."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks on the roadway after leaving the sidewalk at a barrier, but the source maps regions without outlines, so whether and since when ego is past the barrier is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.obstruction_reach","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Reach within which a pedestrian counts as at an obstruction: a walking pedestrian's body width plus one step.","source":"pedestrian body ellipse and walking step length (HCM pedestrian space)"},{"name":"p.sidewalk_return_time","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"Time after a pedestrian has left an obstruction behind within which a return to the sidewalk counts as made as soon as practicable: the walking time, at a design walking speed, to the next point where the sidewalk can be regained.","source":"design walking speed (MUTCD/HCM pedestrian walking speed) and curb-ramp spacing"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_interruption` | a stretch along a sidewalk where no walkable sidewalk exists (a section missing, removed, closed or broken up), carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so a pedestrian's arrival at it is read through st.region_geometry **Not a stand-in for:** an object standing on the sidewalk (st.obstruction) | general","nearest":["st.obstruction: 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user' (a missing section of sidewalk is no object, so the atom leaves out where the duty arises)","st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (the absence of a sidewalk region is not a stretch the source records that a pedestrian meets)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped","role":"subject"},{"id":"b3","text":"or trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"b5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"b8","text":"(1) The person stops","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b9","text":"before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b10","text":"where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b11","text":"or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b12","text":"(2) The person waits for","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b13","text":"two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b14","text":"and the signal does not change","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b15","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b16","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b17","text":"if applicable;","role":"condition"},{"id":"b18","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"b19","text":"(4) The person yields","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b20","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"b21","text":"to pedestrians","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b22","text":"lawfully","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b23","text":"within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b24","text":"and to other traffic","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b25","text":"lawfully","role":"obligation"},{"id":"b26","text":"using the intersection.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red, 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection, the event the words fix it to."},{"span":"b2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motorcycle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels'); 'moped' as DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle that is propelled by a small engine'); each claimed whole. 'A person driving' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.motorcycle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only, to show the shortfall (gap on b3): no definition applies to 'trimobile', and ru.motorcycle ('motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants') leaves out a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side, which the word admits; ru.motor_vehicle would admit every car."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'bicycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'electric bicycle' as DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle ('a device upon which a person may ride ... an electric motor which produces not more than 750 watts'), 'electric scooter' as DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'); each claimed whole."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': the signal controls the approach ego enters through. dev.governs is 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection'; the approach is a carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters: 'a road user's approach to an intersection is a carrier it occupies whose entrance end is that intersection'); its kind is st.travel_region. No halt place is read from dev.governs ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow' is the movement ego makes through the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'; entered and left through rel.occupies): its heading change since entering it (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, which takes the intersection as its region formal) read at the exit, lying in the straight band (neither turn band) or in the turn band opposite a displayed green arrow (dev.traffic_signal green_arrow(dir)): the right band under a left arrow, the left band under a right arrow."},{"span":"b8","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'stops' where a stop is required is DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement', which drv.motion.at_rest carries with the speed tolerance; DEF-NRS-484A-260 states its own scope ('when prohibited') and does not apply to a required stop."},{"span":"b9","atoms":["st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","prim.region_offset_along","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection' is the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking the entrance of the carrier ego approaches through (st.entrance_of: 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks'); 'before entering' is ego short of it along the carrier's direction (sign of prim.region_offset_along) and not overlapping it (rel.occupies), within the stop-point tolerance of it (body-to-mark distance, st.region_geometry). Distance never stands for the association (st.entrance_of 'never inferred from distance')."},{"span":"b10","atoms":["st.stop_line","st.entrance_of","prim.region_offset_along","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made' is the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking the carrier's entrance (st.entrance_of); ego at rest short of it along the carrier's direction (prim.region_offset_along) within the stop-point tolerance (st.region_geometry). A sign that indicates the stop place is read through the line it accompanies (narrowing)."},{"span":"b11","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"'before entering the intersection' is ego at rest at the entrance end of its carrier (st.lane_enters), its footprint not overlapping the intersection (rel.occupies) and within the stop-point tolerance of it (st.region_geometry), where no stop line and no crosswalk marks the carrier ('in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking')."},{"span":"b12","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'waits' is ego remaining at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) at the place of (1), over one stretch of rest."},{"span":"b13","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the applicable official traffic-control device' is the signal head governing ego's carrier (dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs), its official status read from its presence (observable_reading status); 'complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows' are cycles of its displayed states, each complete from one rise of the green turn arrow to its next rise; the number is the law's literal."},{"span":"b14","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the signal does not change' is the same head displaying circular_red facing ego at every observation of the wait: no circular_green for ego's movement."},{"span":"b16","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","prim.conditions_hold"],"derived":[],"justification":"'No other device at the place prohibits the turn' is no dev.regulatory_sign with code no_left_turn, no_right_turn or no_u_turn (the turn made) governing ego's carrier or the intersection (dev.governs, 'at the place') whose conditions hold for ego at the entry (prim.conditions_hold). 'Not a stand-in for: a manoeuvre ... a prohibition sign is a condition' is respected: the turn itself is read by b17."},{"span":"b17","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'if applicable' limits (3) to a turn: ego's heading change since entering the intersection lies in a turn band (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry); proceeding straight through needs no such check."},{"span":"b19","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'yields' is ego holding back: at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) wherever the danger the right-of-way standard bounds would otherwise arise, as the mapping index maps 'shall yield' (NRS_484B_250_1)."},{"span":"b21","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair ...'), read for every road user other than ego."},{"span":"b23","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) that marks the entrance of some carrier (st.entrance_of) entering the intersection ego crosses (st.lane_enters): a crossing tied to the intersection by relation atoms, never by distance."},{"span":"b24","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway'), every road user other than ego."},{"span":"b26","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'using the intersection' is the other road user's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) the intersection ego crosses (st.intersection)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"b20","standard":"the right-of-way (the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence, DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","drv.motion.at_rest"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: DEF-NRS-484A-210 grants the right-of-way against one 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash'; that danger is a projected approach of the centres within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below p.conflict_clearance for traffic, p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance for a pedestrian (prim.closest_approach_distance), which direction, speed and proximity all enter; yielding is being at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) wherever that danger stands.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"b15","why":"The cause of the signal's failure to change (a malfunction, a failed detection) is not observable; the rule reads the red persisting through the two complete cycles, which a working, detecting signal does not show."},{"span":"b22","why":"Whether the pedestrian is lawfully within the crosswalk refers to a pedestrian rule not in the library; the rule owes the yield to every pedestrian within an adjacent crosswalk."},{"span":"b25","why":"Whether other traffic is lawfully using the intersection refers to the verdicts of other rules not composed here; the rule owes the yield to every member of traffic within the intersection."}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"ego is a motorcycle, moped, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter (the admitted aggregates; trimobile: gap on b3). The judged observation is one at which ego leaves an intersection I (ego occupies I at the observation before and not at the judged one), whose last entry took place while ego occupied a carrier c entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) governed by a traffic signal d (dev.governs(d, c) or dev.governs(d, I)) displaying circular_red together with a green turn arrow (green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn)) at that entry observation (read through a since operator from the rise of ego's occupancy of I, no later rise), and ego's heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(ego, I) with p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph), read at the exit, is not in the band of a displayed green turn arrow: it is in the straight band (above the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and below p.left_turn_min_angle), or in the right band (at or below the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and at or above the negative of p.right_turn_max_angle) where green_arrow(left) was displayed, or in the left band (at or above p.left_turn_min_angle and at or below p.left_turn_max_angle) where green_arrow(right) was displayed.","obligation":"For the intersection I, carrier c and signal d selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations), at the judged exit: (1) STOP, by the ontology's approach convention for an act due at a place before an event (rule 4c). The event is ego's entry into I through c. The place is, in the words' order: a stop line recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of(line, c)); where every stop line's entrances are observed and none marks c, a crosswalk recorded as marking c; where neither marks c, c's entrance end at I. The act is ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) short of the place along c's designated direction (sign of prim.region_offset_along with st.lane_direction of c), within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (body-to-mark distance, st.region_geometry), and, for a crosswalk or the intersection, with its footprint not overlapping that region (rel.occupies). The search runs back from the entry observation and ends only at the approach start (the last observation before the entry at which ego, on a carrier the governing mark is recorded as marking, is outside the mark's stopping zone upstream: off it, short of it and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance) or at ego's previous entry into I through such a carrier; nothing else ends it (not the start of the recording, not a first observation, not a distance travelled). Act found: (1) is met; an end reached without it: violated; neither end reached and no act found: unknown. Where a mark's association with c is not observed, whether it governs is unknown, and (1) is unknown unless the verdict is the same at every candidate place. (2) WAIT: within one stretch of rest at the place found in (1) (drv.motion.at_rest held at every observation of the stretch), d displayed circular_red at every observation of it, and the number of rises of d's green turn arrow display since the stretch began (count operator) is at least the literal count of cycles plus one, so that two complete cycles, each from one rise of the arrow to its next, lie within the wait. (3) Where ego turned (heading change since entry in the left band, the right band or the reversal band of p.u_turn_min_angle to p.u_turn_max_angle), no dev.regulatory_sign governing c or I (dev.governs) with code no_left_turn (left band), no_right_turn (right band) or no_u_turn (reversal band) whose conditions hold for ego at the entry (prim.conditions_hold). (4) YIELD: at every observation from the entry to the observation before the exit (a since operator from the entry), ego is at rest, or, for every road user p other than ego that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) occupying a crosswalk w that marks the entrance of a carrier e entering I (st.entrance_of(w, e), st.lane_enters(e, I)), no projected approach within p.conflict_horizon to a centre distance below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance, and, for every road user u other than ego that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying I, no projected approach within p.conflict_horizon to a centre distance below p.conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_within, prim.closest_approach_distance). With no other road user in the scene (4) is met.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.u_turn_min_angle","p.u_turn_max_angle","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b2","why":"'A person driving' (and 'riding', b4) is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"b10","why":"The words are read as listing the stop places in order: the marked stop place, else the near crosswalk, else the intersection. A sign indicating where to stop is read through the stop line it accompanies; a sign with no line is not read.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"b13","why":"The official status of the signal head is read from its presence on the road.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"b20","why":"The danger of a crash that the right-of-way presupposes is read as a projected close approach of the centres under constant velocities.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a motorcycle (ru.motorcycle), approaches intersection I in a lane whose signal shows circular_red with green_arrow(left); it halts at the stop line, waits through only one cycle of the arrow, then proceeds straight through I with no other road user present."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego waits at rest at the stop line while the green arrow rises three times with the circular red steady throughout, then proceeds straight through I; no regulatory sign is present and no pedestrian or other traffic is in a crosswalk of I or in I."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle, in none of the subject aggregates), proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in permit, but the source does not observe the signal head's state, so whether ego entered facing a red with a green turn arrow, and whether it waited through two cycles, is unknown.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"the recording begins with ego already at rest at the stop line of its lane, the signal showing circular_red with green_arrow(left); the arrow rises once in the recording and ego then proceeds straight through I. Whether ego's wait began early enough to cover two complete cycles, and where its approach started, lie before the recording; no recorded act or visible end of the search decides the verdict.","boundary":"the approach start on ego's lane and the beginning of its stretch of rest at the stop line, both before the recording began"},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a bicycle (ru.bicycle), rolls through the crosswalk and into I without halting under circular_red with green_arrow(left), after an observed approach from beyond the stop-point tolerance, and proceeds straight."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a moped (ru.moped), meets (1) and (2) and turns right under a green_arrow(left) while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk across the road it turns into; ego keeps moving and its projected closest approach to the pedestrian falls within the horizon below the pedestrian clearance."}],"literals":[{"span":"b13","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.u_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Heading change at or beyond which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.u_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":210.0,"convention":"Heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which a halt counts as made at the mark, and beyond which the road user is outside the stopping zone.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_250_4_o1 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch (about a half-length plus a half-width of a design passenger car).","source":"design passenger car dimensions; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"b3","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.trimobile` | a motor vehicle designed to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, two of them on one axle, whether ridden astride or seated, as the jurisdiction's taxonomy labels it | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle: 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants' (a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side is not ridden astride, so the atom leaves out road users the permission covers)","ru.motor_vehicle: 'a self-propelled vehicle other than a rail vehicle' (admits every car, which the words do not)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"a3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"a4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a7","text":"but must yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a9","text":"to pedestrians","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a10","text":"lawfully","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a11","text":"within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a12","text":"and to other traffic","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a13","text":"lawfully","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a14","text":"using the intersection.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a15","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red and 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection, the event the words fix it to."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic: 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel'. The law's own qualifier 'vehicular' limits the members the duty reads and leaves out pedestrians (and ridden or herded animals, which no class atom carries): carried beside the aggregate as the condition that ego is not ru.pedestrian ('a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: a person on a bicycle or scooter' is why riders of bicycles and scooters remain vehicular traffic, as paragraph (b) confirms by excepting them."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': the signal controls the approach ego enters through. dev.governs is 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection'; the approach is a carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters: 'a road user's approach to an intersection is a carrier it occupies whose entrance end is that intersection'); its kind is st.travel_region, which dev.governs and st.lane_enters range over. No halt place is read ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"a5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'enter the intersection' is the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges', which carries DEF-NRS-484A-105's 'area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines' and its exclusion of an alley junction), the region the words single out."},{"span":"a6","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'the movement indicated by the green turn arrow' is the turn whose direction the displayed arrow names (dev.traffic_signal green_arrow(dir)); the movement ego makes is its heading change since entering the intersection (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, which takes the intersection as its region formal), read at the exit and bounded by the reading's turn bands: the left band for a left arrow, the right band for a right arrow, the reversal band for a U-turn arrow."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"a2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[{"span":"a15","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about the signal opposing traffic faces: it imposes no duty and states no condition of this one, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"ego is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and not a pedestrian (ru.pedestrian). The judged observation is one at which ego leaves an intersection I (ego occupies I at the observation before and not at the judged one), whose last entry (the rise of ego's occupancy of I with no later rise, read through a since operator) took place while ego occupied a carrier c of kind st.travel_region entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) and a traffic signal d governing c or I (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn) at that entry observation. Exception: not where NRS_484B_307_9b applies to ego (ruleApplies, ego to ego).","obligation":"For the intersection I and signal d selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego's heading change since its entry into I (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(ego, I) with p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph), read at the judged exit, lies in the band of a green turn arrow d displayed at that entry: at or above p.left_turn_min_angle and at or below p.left_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(left) was displayed; at or below the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and at or above the negative of p.right_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(right) was displayed; with magnitude at or above p.u_turn_min_angle and at or below p.u_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(u_turn) was displayed. A heading change in none of the displayed arrows' bands (straight through, or a turn against the arrow) violates the duty.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.u_turn_min_angle","p.u_turn_max_angle"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a6","why":"The movement is read as the heading change through the intersection, from the entry to the exit, against the turn bands of the reading; a movement whose heading change lies in a displayed arrow's band is that arrow's movement whatever lane it ends in.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle, a member of traffic), occupies a left-turn lane entering intersection I; the signal governing the lane displays circular_red with green_arrow(left) as ego enters I; ego crosses I without turning and leaves it with a heading change near zero."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego turns left through I by about a quarter turn and leaves it on the crossing road."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego enters I while the signal governing its lane displays circular_green, and proceeds straight."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not supply yaw rates, so ego's heading change through I is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a moped (ru.moped), enters I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and proceeds straight through: paragraph (b) applies to it and excepts it from this duty."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, enters I under circular_red with green_arrow(right) and turns left through it."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.u_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Heading change at or beyond which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.u_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":210.0,"convention":"Heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"a4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a7","text":"but must yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a8","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"a9","text":"to pedestrians","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a10","text":"lawfully","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a11","text":"within an adjacent crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a12","text":"and to other traffic","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a13","text":"lawfully","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a14","text":"using the intersection.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a15","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red and 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic: 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel'. The qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out pedestrians, carried beside the aggregate as the condition that ego is not ru.pedestrian ('a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'); riders of bicycles and scooters stay in ('Not a stand-in for: a person on a bicycle or scooter')."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': dev.governs ('the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') of the carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters); the carrier's kind is st.travel_region. No halt place is read ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"a5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'enter the intersection' is the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'), the region the words single out."},{"span":"a7","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'must yield' is ego holding back: at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, 'the observable form of a stop') wherever the danger the right-of-way standard bounds would otherwise arise, as the mapping index maps 'shall yield' (NRS_484B_250_1)."},{"span":"a9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrians' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair, or a person on an electric personal assistive mobility device'), read for every road user other than ego."},{"span":"a11","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a crosswalk (st.crosswalk, 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection') that marks the entrance of some carrier (st.entrance_of) entering the intersection ego occupies (st.lane_enters): every crossing of the intersection's approaches, ego's own and those of the roads it turns into, tied to the intersection by relation atoms, never by distance."},{"span":"a12","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"],"derived":[],"justification":"'other traffic' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway'), every road user other than ego."},{"span":"a14","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'using the intersection' is the other road user's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) the intersection ego occupies (st.intersection)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"a8","standard":"the right-of-way (the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence, DEF-NRS-484A-210)","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","drv.motion.at_rest"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"Traffic-conflict technique: DEF-NRS-484A-210 grants the right-of-way against one 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash'; that danger is a projected approach of the centres within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to a centre distance below p.conflict_clearance for traffic, p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance for a pedestrian (prim.closest_approach_distance), which direction, speed and proximity all enter; yielding is being at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) wherever that danger stands.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"a10","why":"Whether the pedestrian is lawfully within the crosswalk refers to a pedestrian rule not in the library; the rule owes the yield to every pedestrian within an adjacent crosswalk."},{"span":"a13","why":"Whether other traffic is lawfully using the intersection refers to the verdicts of other rules not composed here; the rule owes the yield to every member of traffic within the intersection."},{"span":"a15","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about the signal opposing traffic faces: it imposes no duty and states no condition of this one, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"ego is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and not a pedestrian (ru.pedestrian). At the judged observation ego occupies an intersection I, has occupied it at every observation since its last entry into it, and at that entry (the rise of ego's occupancy of I, read through a since operator) ego occupied a carrier c of kind st.travel_region entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) governed by a traffic signal d (dev.governs of c or I) displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn).","obligation":"For the intersection I selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), or both: for every road user p other than ego that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) and occupies a crosswalk w marking the entrance of a carrier e that enters I (st.entrance_of(w, e), st.lane_enters(e, I)), it is not the case that their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) with a centre distance at that closest approach below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and for every road user u other than ego that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and occupies I, the same with p.conflict_clearance. With no such road user in the scene the duty is met.","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a8","why":"The danger of a crash that the right-of-way presupposes is read as a projected close approach of the centres under constant velocities.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, enters intersection I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk across the road it turns into (marking that road's approach carrier into I); ego keeps moving and their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the pedestrian clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego halts within I until the pedestrian has crossed, then completes the turn with no projected approach below the clearance."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego enters I while the signal governing its lane displays circular_green."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the crosswalks mark, so whether the pedestrian's crosswalk is one of I's is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego turns left through I under the arrow with no pedestrian and no other road user in the scene: the duty binds ego alone and is met."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego turns left on the arrow while a car that entered I earlier is still crossing it; ego keeps moving and their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the vehicle clearance."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch (about a half-length plus a half-width of a design passenger car).","source":"design passenger car dimensions; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_413_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-413-2"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"t1","text":"A signal of intention to turn right or left,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t2","text":"or otherwise turn a vehicle from a direct course,","role":"trigger"},{"id":"t3","text":"shall be given continuously during","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t4","text":"not less than the last 100 feet traveled","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t5","text":"in a business or residential district","role":"condition"},{"id":"t6","text":"and not less than the last 300 feet traveled","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t7","text":"in any other area","role":"condition"},{"id":"t8","text":"prior to changing the course of a vehicle.","role":"trigger"},{"id":"t9","text":"This rule shall be observed, regardless of the weather.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"t1","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"A signal 'of intention' is the signal itself: sig.turn_indicator, 'the turn indicator state ∈ {off, left, right}', or sig.hand_signal, 'a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning ∈ {no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter}', the side matching the side of the turn. 'Not a stand-in for: the turn or lane change itself' is respected: the turn is read by its own concept (t2, t8) and the signal is judged separately from it."},{"span":"t2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset","drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset"],"justification":"'turn a vehicle from a direct course', with 'turn right or left' of t1, is a change of the vehicle's heading to one side from an observed onset: drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset or drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset, each recognizing a continuous turning stretch whose heading change reaches the turn angle. 'vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', except 'Devices moved by human power', 'Electric bicycles', electric personal assistive mobility devices and 'An electric scooter'), claimed whole."},{"span":"t3","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"'given continuously' is the matching signal (sig.turn_indicator left or right, or sig.hand_signal left or right) at every observation of the window (a holdsFor window): an observation with the indicator off and no matching arm signal breaks it."},{"span":"t4","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last 100 feet traveled' is a window measured in the distance ego travelled behind the onset (a .path window), read through kin.path_length, 'distance travelled along the body's path since the start of the trace, monotone'; the figure is the law's literal."},{"span":"t6","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last 300 feet traveled' is the same .path window with the law's other literal, through kin.path_length."},{"span":"t8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset","drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset","drv.motion.turning_left","drv.motion.turning_right"],"justification":"'prior to changing the course' places the window before the observed onset of the change: the observation at which drv.motion.turning_left (or drv.motion.turning_right) last became true before the recognition of drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset (or drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset), as those concepts' act records declare it. 'a vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"t5","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."},{"span":"t7","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"t9","why":"The duty holds in every weather: no condition of the weather restricts it, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The judged observation is the recognition of a left turn from an observed onset (drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset with p.left_turn_min_angle, p.turn_yaw_tolerance, p.rest_speed_tolerance, p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) or of a right turn from an observed onset (drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset with p.right_turn_min_angle and the same tolerances).","obligation":"Event, recognition and history (rule 4d): the event is the change of course; it is recognized at the judged observation; its observed onset is the last observation at which drv.motion.turning_left (for a left turn; drv.motion.turning_right for a right turn, each with p.turn_yaw_tolerance and p.rest_speed_tolerance) became true, the turning state having held at every observation since (a since operator: turning since (rise of turning and W)). W, read at that onset: where asm.business_or_residence_district holds there, at every observation of the window of the literal 100 ft of path travelled by ego behind the onset (holdsFor .path, kin.path_length), ego's turn indicator is left (sig.turn_indicator = left) or its arm signal means left (sig.hand_signal = left); where it does not hold, the same over the window of the literal 300 ft. For a right turn the matching side is right. The window ends at the onset and is the words' own bound; a window that reaches past the start of the recording is unknown (windowTruncated), as is the duty where the assumption is undeclared and the two windows decide differently. Conduct after the onset is not read.","params":["p.left_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.turn_yaw_tolerance","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"t1","why":"A change of course is read as a turn whose heading change from its observed onset reaches the turn angle; a lane change or a gentle departure from the course, whose heading change stays below it, is not read, and a road bend followed through that angle in one turning stretch is read as a turn.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, with the business-or-residence-district assumption declared, drives along a straight roadway and turns left at an intersection; its left indicator lights only over the final few metres before the turn begins, so at the onset the window of the last 100 ft holds observations with the indicator off and no arm signal."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but the left indicator is lit at every observation over well more than the last 100 ft travelled before the turn's onset."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego drives straight along a straight roadway and makes no turn."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not observe turn indicators and observes no arm signal, so whether a signal was given is unknown.","masked":["sig.turn_indicator"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego turns right with the assumption declared false (any other area); its right indicator is lit over the last 100 ft before the onset but not over the last 300 ft."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego, the assumption declared, turns left with its indicator off but its arm signal meaning left at every observation over the last 100 ft before the onset."}],"literals":[{"span":"t4","text":"100 feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"t6","text":"300 feet","value":300,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.turn_yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","value":5.0,"convention":"Yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none: above lane-keeping yaw noise, below the yaw rates of turning at a junction.","source":"vehicle yaw-rate noise and junction turning rates; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e4","text":"any vehicle,","role":"subject"},{"id":"e5","text":"whether attended or unattended,","role":"condition"},{"id":"e6","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e7","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"standard"},{"id":"e8","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e9","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway opposite a standing vehicle shall be left","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e10","text":"for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e11","text":"and a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway is 'the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders', carrying DEF-NRS-484A-095 ('the entire width between the boundary lines of every way dedicated to a public authority'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies). 'Not a stand-in for: the roadway' is respected: the part of it the duty reads is e6."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.human_direction","dev.governs"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'stop' where prohibited is DEF-NRS-484A-260, 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device'; 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155) and 'standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-250) are halts too, so their union is a halt (drv.motion.at_rest) other than the excepted ones, which the rule carries beside it: a halt behind a road user ahead in ego's lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) that is itself at rest within p.queue_gap (rel.surface_gap), or a halt while a stop indication governs ego's carrier (dev.governs of a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red or a red_arrow, a dev.stop_sign, or a dev.human_direction indicating stop). 'no person shall' is read through the vehicle's halt (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"e4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', with its exceptions), claimed whole."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.shoulder","st.on_way"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the paved or main-traveled part of the highway': the main-traveled part is the roadway (st.roadway, 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder'), the paved part also a shoulder whose paved attribute holds (st.shoulder, 'paved attribute'); ego's footprint overlaps one (rel.occupies) lying on the highway of e1 (st.on_way)."},{"span":"e13","atoms":["sig.hazard","kin.engine_running"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on e13): that a vehicle is disabled so that it cannot avoid stopping is a condition of the vehicle no atom carries; hazard lamps (sig.hazard, 'both indicators flashing together') are a lamp state, and an engine stopped (kin.engine_running) is 'Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt' nor for a vehicle that cannot move."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e7","standard":"practicable","concepts":["drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.shoulder","st.parking_space","rel.occupies"],"params":["p.offroad_stop_reach"],"convention":"Off-road standing place within braking reach: halting off the paved or main-traveled part is practicable where a region off it lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of the halted vehicle's body (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry): a shoulder whose paved attribute does not hold (st.shoulder) or a parking space (st.parking_space) that does not overlap the roadway. The distance to the nearest such place enters the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"e5","why":"Whether the vehicle is attended or unattended does not change the duty: it is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a vehicle; at the judged observation ego occupies a roadway, or a shoulder whose paved attribute holds, lying on a highway (st.on_way), asm.business_or_residence_district does not hold there, and ego is halted (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) other than behind a road user ahead in its lane at rest within p.queue_gap or under a stop indication governing its carrier. Exception: a disabled vehicle (gap on e13).","obligation":"It is not the case that a region off the paved or main-traveled part (a shoulder whose paved attribute does not hold, or a parking space not overlapping the roadway) lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of ego's body (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry).","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.queue_gap","p.offroad_stop_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e3","why":"'no person shall' is read through the vehicle's halt, whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e7","why":"Practicability is read only through an off-road standing place within reach; its size and surface are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway of a rural highway, the assumption declared false, with an unpaved shoulder beside it within the reach and no road user ahead."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway of a rural highway where no unpaved shoulder or parking space lies within the reach."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway with the business-or-residence-district assumption declared true."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source maps regions without outlines, so the distance to the shoulder is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.queue_gap","unit":"m","value":10.0,"convention":"Gap to a halted road user ahead in the lane within which a halt counts as made to avoid conflict with it: a queued vehicle's standstill spacing plus a margin.","source":"queue standstill spacing (HCM)"},{"name":"p.offroad_stop_reach","unit":"m","value":30.0,"convention":"Distance within which an off-road standing place counts as practicable for a halting vehicle: the braking distance of a moderate approach, within which the driver can halt on it instead.","source":"stopping-distance model (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"e13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, crash damage, a lost wheel or a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a halt, hazard lamps lit or an engine stopped | general","nearest":["sig.hazard: 'both indicators flashing together' (a lamp state, not whether the vehicle can move)","kin.engine_running: 'Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt' (a stopped engine is no disablement, and a disabled vehicle may run its engine)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e4","text":"any vehicle,","role":"subject"},{"id":"e5","text":"whether attended or unattended,","role":"condition"},{"id":"e6","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e7","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e8","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e9","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway opposite a standing vehicle shall be left","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e10","text":"for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"standard"},{"id":"e11","text":"and a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway is 'the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders' (DEF-NRS-484A-095); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.human_direction","dev.governs"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"As in NRS_484B_440_1_o1: the halt of DEF-