assage_width"],"convention":"Narrow-lane width of highway design guides: the free strip opposite the standing vehicle lets another vehicle pass where its width (st.lane_width) is at or above p.free_passage_width, a design vehicle's width plus lateral clearance; the strip's measured width enters the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"e5","why":"Whether the vehicle is attended or unattended does not change the duty: it is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_440_1_o1, whether or not an off-road place is within reach: ego is a vehicle halted (as read there) on a roadway or a paved shoulder of a highway where asm.business_or_residence_district does not hold. Exception: a disabled vehicle (gap on e13).","obligation":"Some lane l lying on the same highway as the region ego occupies (st.on_way), not occupied by ego, has a width (st.lane_width) at or above p.free_passage_width, and no road user other than ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) occupies l with a longitudinal overlap with ego (rel.longitudinal_overlap) at or above zero.","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.queue_gap","p.free_passage_width"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e9","why":"The unobstructed width is read as a free lane beside the standing vehicle; a width made up of a part-lane and a shoulder, and an obstruction that is no road user, are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego halts in its lane of a two-lane rural highway, the assumption declared false, while a truck stands halted in the opposite lane alongside it."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego halts in its lane; the opposite lane is of ordinary width and free."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego drives along the rural highway without halting."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in permit, but the source does not observe lane widths.","masked":["st.lane_width"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.queue_gap","unit":"m","value":10.0,"convention":"Gap to a halted road user ahead in the lane within which a halt counts as made to avoid conflict with it: a queued vehicle's standstill spacing plus a margin.","source":"queue standstill spacing (HCM)"},{"name":"p.free_passage_width","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Width of a free strip beside a standing vehicle that lets another vehicle pass: a design vehicle's width plus lateral clearance (narrow-lane width of highway design guides).","source":"AASHTO Green Book lane widths"}],"gaps":[{"span":"e13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, crash damage, a lost wheel or a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a halt, hazard lamps lit or an engine stopped | general","nearest":["sig.hazard: 'both indicators flashing together' (a lamp state, not whether the vehicle can move)","kin.engine_running: 'Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt' (a stopped engine is no disablement)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
