egion_lateral_offset of o of the same sign as that of s and of smaller magnitude) and the distance from ego's body to o is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin.","params":["p.pedestrian_edge_margin","p.obstruction_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s14","why":"'impassable' is read only through a physical object between the bicycle lane and the sidewalk; a strip impassable for other reasons (standing vehicles, a drop-off) is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks down the middle of the adjacent lane, well beyond the edge margin from both the sidewalk and the barrier."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks along the roadway hugging the barrier's outer side, within the edge margin of it, then of the sidewalk."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego stays on the sidewalk throughout."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks in the roadway after leaving the sidewalk at a barrier, but the source maps regions without outlines, so ego's distance to the sidewalk and to the barrier is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego walks in a bicycle lane beside a strip of excavation that lies between the lane and the sidewalk within the reach: exception (c) applies."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.pedestrian_edge_margin","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"Lateral body-to-edge distance within which a pedestrian walking on the highway counts as at the side next to the sidewalk or the obstruction: a step's width plus the shy distance a walker keeps from a curb or an object