s","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', carrying DEF-NRS-484A-240 ('intended for the use of pedestrians'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies), read at the earlier observation at which ego met the obstruction."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"st.obstruction is 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'; 'encounters' is ego at the obstruction while on the sidewalk: drv.position.near_region(ego, o) with p.obstruction_reach over st.region_geometry, the anchor of the obstruction to ego."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on s4): a missing section of sidewalk is no 'physical object' (st.obstruction), and the absence of a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk) is not a stretch a source records that a pedestrian meets."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed' is ego's travel off the sidewalk: its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a region of kind st.travel_region, which excludes 'a sidewalk'."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway","st.on_way","st.travel_region","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the immediately adjacent highway' is the same way as the sidewalk: the travel region ego occupies and the sidewalk both lie on one highway region (st.on_way); belonging is never read from a distance."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk","st.obstruction"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"A purpose read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): since the last observation at which ego occupied the sidewalk while at that obstruction, ego has occupied no sidewalk."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such a pedestrian' is the pedestrian of s1: the same binder and aggregate."},{"span":"s16","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'return to the sidewalk' is ego's footprint again overlapping (rel.occupies) a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk, 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line')."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s17","standard":"as soon as practicable","concepts":["drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.obstruction"],"params":["p.obstruction_reach","p.sidewalk_return_time"],"convention":"A return is practicable once the obstruction is behind the pedestrian: from the observation at which ego ceased to be at the obstruction (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach no longer holds; Term.sinceRise of its negation), ego is to be back on a sidewalk before p.sidewalk_return_time has elapsed, the walking time at a design walking speed to the next point where the sidewalk can be regained. The time elapsed since passing the obstruction enters the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s12","why":"A permission to walk in either direction on the highway: the duty to return to the sidewalk is the same in either direction, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_297_6_o1: ego is a pedestrian; at the judged observation ego occupies no sidewalk and occupies a travel region lying on a highway h on which a sidewalk s also lies, and since the last observation at which ego occupied s while at an obstruction o (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), ego has occupied no sidewalk.","obligation":"For the obstruction o selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego is at o (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), or the time since ego ceased to be at o (Term.sinceRise of not drv.position.near_region(ego, o)) is below p.sidewalk_return_time. Once ego occupies a sidewalk again the applicability no longer holds.","params":["p.obstruction_reach","p.sidewalk_return_time"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s17","why":"'as soon as practicable' is read as a return within a fixed time after the obstruction is behind the pedestrian; a sidewalk that stays blocked beyond the obstruction is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier, passes it on the roadway, and keeps walking on the roadway beside a free sidewalk long after the barrier is behind it."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier, passes it on the roadway and steps back onto the sidewalk shortly after the barrier is behind it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego stays on the sidewalk throughout."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks on the roadway after leaving the sidewalk at a barrier, but the source maps regions without outlines, so whether and since when ego is past the barrier is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.obstruction_reach","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Reach within which a pedestrian counts as at an obstruction: a walking pedestrian's body width plus one step.","source":"pedestrian body ellipse and walking step length (HCM pedestrian space)"},{"name":"p.sidewalk_return_time","unit":"s","value":10.0,"convention":"Time after a pedestrian has left an obstruction behind within which a return to the sidewalk counts as made as soon as practicable: the walking time, at a design walking speed, to the next point where the sidewalk can be regained.","source":"design walking speed (MUTCD/HCM pedestrian walking speed) and curb-ramp spacing"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_interruption` | a stretch along a sidewalk where no walkable sidewalk exists (a section missing, removed, closed or broken up), carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so a pedestrian's arrival at it is read through st.region_geometry **Not a stand-in for:** an object standing on the sidewalk (st.obstruction) | general","nearest":["st.obstruction: 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user' (a missing section of sidewalk is no object, so the atom leaves out where the duty arises)","st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (the absence of a sidewalk region is not a stretch the source records that a pedestrian meets)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped","role":"subject"},{"id":"b3","text":"or trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"b5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c1","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c2","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c3","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c4","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c5","text":"if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c6","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c7","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red, 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection, the event the words fix it to."},{"span":"b2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motorcycle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver and designed to travel on not more than three wheels'); 'moped' as DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle that is propelled by a small engine'); each claimed whole. 'A person driving' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.motorcycle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only, to show the shortfall (gap on b3): no definition applies to 'trimobile', and ru.motorcycle ('motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants') leaves out a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side, which the word admits; ru.motor_vehicle would admit every car."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'bicycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'electric bicycle' as DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle ('a device upon which a person may ride ... an electric motor which produces not more than 750 watts'), 'electric scooter' as DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'); each claimed whole."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': the signal controls the approach ego enters through. dev.governs is 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection'; the approach is a carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters: 'a road user's approach to an intersection is a carrier it occupies whose entrance end is that intersection'); its kind is st.travel_region. No halt place is read from dev.governs ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow' is the movement ego makes through the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'; entered and left through rel.occupies): its heading change since entering it (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, which takes the intersection as its region formal) read at the exit, lying in the straight band (neither turn band) or in the turn band opposite a displayed green arrow (dev.traffic_signal green_arrow(dir)): the right band under a left arrow, the left band under a right arrow."},{"span":"c1","atoms":["st.stop_line","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","prim.region_offset_along","st.region_geometry","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'stops' where a stop is required is DEF-NRS-484A-255, 'complete cessation from movement', carried by drv.motion.at_rest (DEF-NRS-484A-260 states its own scope, 'when prohibited', and does not apply). The places, in the words' order: 'where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made' is the stop line (st.stop_line, 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt for a device') recorded as marking the entrance of ego's carrier (st.entrance_of, 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks'); 'the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection' is the crosswalk (st.crosswalk) recorded as marking that entrance; 'before entering the intersection' is the carrier's entrance end (st.lane_enters). 'before entering' is ego short of the place along the carrier's direction (sign of prim.region_offset_along), its footprint not overlapping a crosswalk or the intersection (rel.occupies), within the stop-point tolerance (body-to-mark distance, st.region_geometry). The association is never inferred from distance."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"ego is a motorcycle, moped, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter (the admitted aggregates; trimobile: gap on b3). The judged observation is one at which ego leaves an intersection I (ego occupies I at the observation before and not at the judged one), whose last entry (the rise of ego's occupancy of I with no later rise, read through a since operator) took place while ego occupied a carrier c entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) governed by a traffic signal d (dev.governs(d, c) or dev.governs(d, I)) displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn) at that entry observation; and ego's heading change since that entry (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(ego, I) with p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph), read at the exit, is not in the band of a displayed green turn arrow: it is in the straight band (above the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and below p.left_turn_min_angle), or in the right band (at or below the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and at or above the negative of p.right_turn_max_angle) where green_arrow(left) was displayed, or in the left band (at or above p.left_turn_min_angle and at or below p.left_turn_max_angle) where green_arrow(right) was displayed.","obligation":"Rule 4c, by the ontology's approach convention for an act due at a place before an event. For I, c and d selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations), at the judged exit: the event is ego's entry into I through c (the rise of ego's occupancy of I). The place is, in the words' order: a stop line recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of(line, c)); where every stop line's entrances are observed and none marks c, a crosswalk recorded as marking c; where neither marks c, c's entrance end at I. The act is ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) short of the place along c's designated direction (sign of prim.region_offset_along with st.lane_direction of c), within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (body-to-mark distance, st.region_geometry), and, for a crosswalk or the intersection, with its footprint not overlapping that region (rel.occupies). The search runs back from the entry observation and ends only at the approach start (the last observation before the entry at which ego, on a carrier the governing mark is recorded as marking, is outside the mark's stopping zone upstream: off it, short of it and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance) or at ego's previous entry into I through such a carrier; nothing else ends it (not the start of the recording, not a first observation, not a distance travelled). Act found: met; an end reached without the act: violated; neither end reached and no act found: unknown. Where a mark's association with c is not observed, whether it governs is unknown, and the duty is unknown unless the verdict is the same at every candidate place.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b2","why":"'A person driving' (and 'riding', b4) is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle's conduct whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c1","why":"The words are read as listing the stop places in order: the marked stop place, else the near crosswalk, else the intersection. A sign indicating where to stop is read through the stop line it accompanies; a sign with no line is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a bicycle (ru.bicycle), approaches intersection I from beyond the stop-point tolerance on a lane whose stop line is recorded, under circular_red with green_arrow(left); it rolls across the line and the crosswalk into I without halting and proceeds straight."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego, a motorcycle (ru.motorcycle), halts short of the stop line within the tolerance, then proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left)."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle, in none of the subject aggregates), proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the stop line and crosswalk mark, so the governing place is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"the recording begins with ego already on its lane inside the stopping zone of the stop line, moving slowly; it then proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) without a recorded halt. Its approach start lies before the recording, and no recorded act or visible end of the search decides the verdict.","boundary":"the approach start on ego's lane, before the recording began"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Stop-point tolerance of the ontology's approach convention: the body-to-mark distance within which a halt counts as made at the mark, and beyond which the road user is outside the stopping zone.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_250_4_o1 this iteration"}],"gaps":[{"span":"b3","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.trimobile` | a motor vehicle designed to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, two of them on one axle, whether ridden astride or seated, as the jurisdiction's taxonomy labels it | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle: 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants' (a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side is not ridden astride, so the atom leaves out road users the permission covers)","ru.motor_vehicle: 'a self-propelled vehicle other than a rail vehicle' (admits every car, which the words do not)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped","role":"subject"},{"id":"b3","text":"or trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"b5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c1","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c2","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c3","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"condition"},{"id":"c4","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c5","text":"if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c6","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c7","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red, 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection."},{"span":"b2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motorcycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver'); 'moped' as DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle'); each claimed whole. 'A person driving' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.motorcycle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only, to show the shortfall (gap on b3): ru.motorcycle ('motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants') leaves out a trimobile seated in a cabin or side by side."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'bicycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), 'electric bicycle' as DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle, 'electric scooter' as DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'); each claimed whole."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': dev.governs ('the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') of the carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters); the carrier's kind is st.travel_region."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The movement through the intersection (st.intersection, entered and left through rel.occupies): ego's heading change since entering it (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, region formal the intersection), read at the exit, in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed green arrow (dev.traffic_signal green_arrow(dir))."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'waits' is ego remaining at rest (drv.motion.at_rest) over one stretch before its entry, on its approach carrier (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters) and outside the intersection (st.intersection). 'the applicable official traffic-control device' is the signal head governing that carrier (dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs), its official status read from its presence (observable_reading status); 'complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows' are cycles of its displayed states, each complete from one rise of the green turn arrow to its next rise, the number being the law's literal; 'the signal does not change' is the same head displaying circular_red at every observation of the wait."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"The cause of the signal's not changing (a malfunction, a failed detection) adds no restriction the rule could observe beyond c2: a red that persists while the arrow completes two cycles is what a malfunctioning or non-detecting signal shows, and a working, detecting signal does not show it, so the duty is the same whether or not these words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"The same as NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: ego is one of the admitted classes; judged at ego's exit from an intersection I entered through a carrier c governed by a signal d that displayed circular_red with a green turn arrow at the entry, ego's heading change since that entry lying in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed arrow.","obligation":"For I, c and d selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations), at the judged exit: before the entry, there was a stretch of observations at each of which ego was at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), occupied c and did not occupy I, such that d displayed circular_red at every observation of the stretch and the number of rises of d's green turn arrow display since the stretch began (count operator) is at least the literal count of cycles plus one, so that two complete cycles, each from one rise of the arrow to its next, lie within the wait. The search for the stretch runs back from the entry and ends at the observation at which ego's occupancy of c last became true or at ego's previous entry into I; a stretch whose beginning lies before the recording leaves the count unknown, and with no qualifying stretch found and neither end reached the duty is unknown.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b2","why":"'A person driving' (and 'riding', b4) is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c2","why":"The official status of the signal head is read from its presence on the road; the wait is read as one unbroken stretch of rest on the approach.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a motorcycle (ru.motorcycle), arrives on its lane, halts at the stop line under circular_red, waits while the green left arrow rises only twice, then proceeds straight through I."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego halts at the stop line and stays at rest while the green left arrow rises three times with the circular red steady throughout, then proceeds straight through I."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a motorcycle, turns left through I with the green left arrow."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in permit, but the source does not observe the signal head's state.","masked":["dev.traffic_signal"]},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"the recording begins with ego already at rest at the stop line under circular_red; the arrow rises twice in the recording and ego then proceeds straight through I. When its stretch of rest began lies before the recording, so the count of cycles is not decided.","boundary":"the beginning of ego's stretch of rest on its lane, before the recording began"}],"literals":[{"span":"c2","text":"two","value":2,"unit":"count"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[{"span":"b3","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.trimobile` | a motor vehicle designed to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, two of them on one axle, whether ridden astride or seated, as the jurisdiction's taxonomy labels it | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle: 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants' (a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side is not ridden astride, so the atom leaves out road users the permission covers)","ru.motor_vehicle: 'a self-propelled vehicle other than a rail vehicle' (admits every car, which the words do not)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o3","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped","role":"subject"},{"id":"b3","text":"or trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"b5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c1","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c2","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c3","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c4","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c5","text":"if applicable;","role":"condition"},{"id":"c6","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c7","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); read at ego's entry into the intersection."},{"span":"b2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motorcycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver'); 'moped' as DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle'); each claimed whole; 'driving' read through controlled motion."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.motorcycle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only, to show the shortfall (gap on b3): ru.motorcycle ('motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants') leaves out a trimobile seated in a cabin or side by side."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'bicycle', 'electric bicycle', 'electric scooter' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'); each claimed whole."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': dev.governs of the carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters); its kind is st.travel_region."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The movement through the intersection (st.intersection, rel.occupies): ego's heading change since entering it (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry), read at the exit, in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed green arrow (dev.traffic_signal)."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","prim.conditions_hold"],"derived":[],"justification":"'No other device at the place prohibits the turn' is no dev.regulatory_sign ('a point regulation by catalogue code') with code no_left_turn, no_right_turn or no_u_turn, matching the turn made, governing ego's carrier or the intersection (dev.governs: 'at the place') whose conditions hold for ego at the entry (prim.conditions_hold). Its exclusion 'a prohibition sign is a condition' is respected: the turn is read by c5."},{"span":"c5","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'if applicable' limits the duty to a turn: ego's heading change since entering the intersection lies in a turn band (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry); proceeding straight through needs no such check."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"The same as NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 (ego of the admitted classes, judged at its exit from an intersection I entered through a carrier c under a signal d displaying circular_red with a green turn arrow, its heading change since the entry in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed arrow), and, by c5, that heading change lies in a turn band: the right band, the left band, or the reversal band (magnitude at or above p.u_turn_min_angle and at or below p.u_turn_max_angle).","obligation":"For I and c selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): no dev.regulatory_sign governing c or I (dev.governs) carries code no_left_turn where the heading change lies in the left band, no_right_turn where it lies in the right band, or no_u_turn where it lies in the reversal band, with its conditions holding for ego at the entry observation (prim.conditions_hold, read through a since operator from the entry).","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.u_turn_min_angle","p.u_turn_max_angle"],"narrowings":[{"span":"c4","why":"'other device' is read through regulatory signs whose code prohibits the turn made; a lane-use marking or an overhead lane-control signal is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a moped (ru.moped), turns right through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) while a no_right_turn sign with no conditions governs its lane."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego turns right under circular_red with green_arrow(left) with no regulatory sign governing its lane or I."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a moped, proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left): no turn is made."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not observe what devices govern, so whether the sign governs ego's lane is unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.u_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Heading change at or beyond which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.u_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":210.0,"convention":"Heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"}],"gaps":[{"span":"b3","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.trimobile` | a motor vehicle designed to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, two of them on one axle, whether ridden astride or seated, as the jurisdiction's taxonomy labels it | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle: 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants' (a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side is not ridden astride, so the atom leaves out road users the permission covers)","ru.motor_vehicle: 'a self-propelled vehicle other than a rail vehicle' (admits every car, which the words do not)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o4","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9b"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"b1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b2","text":"A person driving a motorcycle, moped","role":"subject"},{"id":"b3","text":"or trimobile","role":"subject"},{"id":"b4","text":"or riding a bicycle, an electric bicycle or an electric scooter","role":"subject"},{"id":"b5","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b6","text":"may proceed straight through or turn in the direction opposite that indicated by the green turn arrow","role":"trigger"},{"id":"b7","text":"if:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c1","text":"(1) The person stops before entering the crosswalk on the nearest side of the intersection where the sign or pavement marking indicates where the stop must be made or, in the absence of any such crosswalk, sign or marking, before entering the intersection;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c2","text":"(2) The person waits for two complete cycles of the lights or lighted arrows of the applicable official traffic-control device and the signal does not change","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c3","text":"because of a malfunction or because the signal failed to detect the presence of the motorcycle, moped, trimobile, bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c4","text":"(3) No other device at the place prohibits the turn,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c5","text":"if applicable;","role":"sibling"},{"id":"c6","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"c7","text":"(4) The person yields the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"b1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); read at ego's entry into the intersection."},{"span":"b2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motorcycle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle ('every motor vehicle equipped with a seat or saddle for the use of the driver'); 'moped' as DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped ('a motor-driven scooter, motor-driven cycle or similar vehicle'); each claimed whole; 'driving' read through controlled motion."},{"span":"b3","atoms":["ru.motorcycle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only, to show the shortfall (gap on b3): ru.motorcycle ('motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants') leaves out a trimobile seated in a cabin or side by side."},{"span":"b4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'bicycle', 'electric bicycle', 'electric scooter' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle ('a device propelled by human power upon which a person may ride'), DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle and DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter ('a vehicle with handlebars and an electric motor'); each claimed whole."},{"span":"b5","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': dev.governs of the carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters); its kind is st.travel_region."},{"span":"b6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection","dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"The movement through the intersection (st.intersection, rel.occupies): ego's heading change since entering it (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry), read at the exit, in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed green arrow (dev.traffic_signal)."},{"span":"c7","atoms":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'yields the right-of-way': DEF-NRS-484A-210 makes the right-of-way the right to proceed in preference to one 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence'; yielding is ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, as the mapping index maps 'shall yield') wherever that danger stands, read as a projected approach of the centres within the horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to below the clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance). 'pedestrians' is DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot ...'); 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a crosswalk (st.crosswalk) that marks the entrance (st.entrance_of) of a carrier (st.travel_region) entering the intersection ego crosses (st.lane_enters), tied by relation atoms, never by distance; 'other traffic' is DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic ('pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ...') other than ego, 'using the intersection' its footprint overlapping the intersection (st.intersection). 'lawfully' is not read (narrowing)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-135::motorcycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-125::moped","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-025::bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-017::electric_bicycle","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484B-018::electric_scooter"]}],"applicability":"The same as NRS_484B_307_9b_o1: ego of the admitted classes, judged at its exit from an intersection I entered through a carrier c under a signal d displaying circular_red with a green turn arrow at the entry, its heading change since the entry lying in the straight band or in the turn band opposite a displayed arrow.","obligation":"For I selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): at every observation from the entry into I to the observation before the judged exit (a since operator from the entry), ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), or both: for every road user p other than ego that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) and occupies a crosswalk w marking the entrance of a carrier e that enters I (st.entrance_of(w, e), st.lane_enters(e, I)), it is not the case that their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) with a centre distance at that closest approach below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and for every road user u other than ego that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and occupies I, the same with p.conflict_clearance. With no other road user in the scene the duty is met.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"b2","why":"'A person driving' (and 'riding', b4) is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c7","why":"The danger of a crash the right-of-way presupposes is read as a projected close approach of the centres under constant velocities; 'lawfully' is not read, so the yield is owed to every pedestrian within an adjacent crosswalk and every member of traffic within the intersection (the lawfulness of their presence refers to rules not in the library).","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a moped (ru.moped), proceeds straight through I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) while a pedestrian walks in the far-side crosswalk of I; ego keeps moving and their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the pedestrian clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego halts within I until the pedestrian has crossed, then proceeds with no projected approach below the clearance."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a moped, turns left through I with the green left arrow."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the crosswalks mark.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego proceeds straight through I under the red with a left arrow with no other road user in the scene: the duty binds ego alone and is met."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch (about a half-length plus a half-width of a design passenger car).","source":"design passenger car dimensions; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"b3","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.trimobile` | a motor vehicle designed to travel on three wheels in contact with the ground, two of them on one axle, whether ridden astride or seated, as the jurisdiction's taxonomy labels it | local","nearest":["ru.motorcycle: 'motor vehicle on two or three wheels ridden astride, including three-wheeled variants' (a three-wheeler seated in a cabin or side by side is not ridden astride, so the atom leaves out road users the permission covers)","ru.motor_vehicle: 'a self-propelled vehicle other than a rail vehicle' (admits every car, which the words do not)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"reference"},{"id":"a3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"a4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a7","text":"but must yield the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a8","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': a steady red with a green turn arrow is circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red and 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection, the event the words fix it to."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic: 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel'. The law's own qualifier 'vehicular' limits the members the duty reads and leaves out pedestrians (and ridden or herded animals, which no class atom carries): carried beside the aggregate as the condition that ego is not ru.pedestrian ('a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: a person on a bicycle or scooter' is why riders of bicycles and scooters remain vehicular traffic, as paragraph (b) confirms by excepting them."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': the signal controls the approach ego enters through. dev.governs is 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection'; the approach is a carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters: 'a road user's approach to an intersection is a carrier it occupies whose entrance end is that intersection'); its kind is st.travel_region, which dev.governs and st.lane_enters range over. No halt place is read ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"a5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'enter the intersection' is the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges', which carries DEF-NRS-484A-105's 'area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines' and its exclusion of an alley junction), the region the words single out."},{"span":"a6","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"],"justification":"'the movement indicated by the green turn arrow' is the turn whose direction the displayed arrow names (dev.traffic_signal green_arrow(dir)); the movement ego makes is its heading change since entering the intersection (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, which takes the intersection as its region formal), read at the exit and bounded by the reading's turn bands: the left band for a left arrow, the right band for a right arrow, the reversal band for a U-turn arrow."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"a2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"a2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o2","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"a2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o3","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"exception"},{"span":"a2","rule":"NRS_484B_307_9b_o4","map":{"ego":"ego"},"as":"exception"}],"residues":[{"span":"a8","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about the signal opposing traffic faces: it imposes no duty and states no condition of this one, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"ego is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and not a pedestrian (ru.pedestrian). The judged observation is one at which ego leaves an intersection I (ego occupies I at the observation before and not at the judged one), whose last entry (the rise of ego's occupancy of I with no later rise, read through a since operator) took place while ego occupied a carrier c of kind st.travel_region entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) and a traffic signal d governing c or I (dev.governs) displayed circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn) at that entry observation. Exception: not where any node of paragraph (b) applies to ego (ruleApplies NRS_484B_307_9b_o1 to _o4, ego to ego; they share one applicability).","obligation":"For the intersection I and signal d selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego's heading change since its entry into I (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry(ego, I) with p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph), read at the judged exit, lies in the band of a green turn arrow d displayed at that entry: at or above p.left_turn_min_angle and at or below p.left_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(left) was displayed; at or below the negative of p.right_turn_min_angle and at or above the negative of p.right_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(right) was displayed; with magnitude at or above p.u_turn_min_angle and at or below p.u_turn_max_angle where green_arrow(u_turn) was displayed. A heading change in none of the displayed arrows' bands (straight through, or a turn against the arrow) violates the duty.","params":["p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph","p.left_turn_min_angle","p.left_turn_max_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_max_angle","p.u_turn_min_angle","p.u_turn_max_angle"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a6","why":"The movement is read as the heading change through the intersection, from the entry to the exit, against the turn bands of the reading; a movement whose heading change lies in a displayed arrow's band is that arrow's movement whatever lane it ends in.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car (ru.motor_vehicle, a member of traffic), occupies a left-turn lane entering intersection I; the signal governing the lane displays circular_red with green_arrow(left) as ego enters I; ego crosses I without turning and leaves it with a heading change near zero."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego turns left through I by about a quarter turn and leaves it on the crossing road."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego enters I while the signal governing its lane displays circular_green, and proceeds straight."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not supply yaw rates, so ego's heading change through I is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego, a moped (ru.moped), enters I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and proceeds straight through: paragraph (b) applies to it and excepts it from this duty."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, enters I under circular_red with green_arrow(right) and turns left through it."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.left_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a left turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed (a U-turn).","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.right_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Upper bound of a right turn, above which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.u_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":150.0,"convention":"Heading change at or beyond which the direction of travel counts as reversed.","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.u_turn_max_angle","unit":"deg","value":210.0,"convention":"Heading change beyond which the road user has turned past the opposite direction (a loop rather than a reversal).","source":"proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_307_9a_o2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-307-9a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"a1","text":"Where the signal is a steady red with a green turn arrow:","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a2","text":"Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (b) [NRS-484B-307-9b],","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a3","text":"vehicular traffic","role":"subject"},{"id":"a4","text":"facing the signal","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a5","text":"may enter the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"a6","text":"only to make the movement indicated by the green turn arrow,","role":"sibling"},{"id":"a7","text":"but must yield the right-of-way to pedestrians lawfully within an adjacent crosswalk and to other traffic lawfully using the intersection.","role":"obligation"},{"id":"a8","text":"Drivers turning in the direction of the arrow are thereby advised that so long as the turn arrow is illuminated, oncoming or opposing traffic simultaneously faces a steady red signal.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"a1","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.traffic_signal is 'a signal head; state ∈ {..., circular_red, green_arrow(dir), ...}' and 'several states may be displayed at once': circular_red displayed together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn); 'steady' excludes flashing_red and 'turn' excludes green_arrow(straight). Read at ego's entry into the intersection."},{"span":"a3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic: 'pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances ... using any highway for purposes of travel'. The qualifier 'vehicular' leaves out pedestrians, carried beside the aggregate as the condition that ego is not ru.pedestrian ('a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'); riders of bicycles and scooters stay in ('Not a stand-in for: a person on a bicycle or scooter')."},{"span":"a4","atoms":["dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'facing the signal': dev.governs ('the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') of the carrier ego occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters); the carrier's kind is st.travel_region. No halt place is read ('Not a stand-in for: a position')."},{"span":"a5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'enter the intersection' is the observation at which ego's footprint comes to overlap (rel.occupies) the intersection (st.intersection, 'the region where two roadways meet'), the region the words single out."},{"span":"a7","atoms":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","st.intersection","st.travel_region"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'must yield the right-of-way': DEF-NRS-484A-210 makes the right-of-way the right to proceed in preference to one 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence'; yielding is ego at rest (drv.motion.at_rest, as the mapping index maps 'shall yield') wherever that danger stands, read as a projected approach of the centres within the horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) to below the clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance). 'pedestrians' is DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian ('a person afoot, a person in a manual or motorized wheelchair ...'); 'within an adjacent crosswalk' is the pedestrian's footprint overlapping (rel.occupies) a crosswalk (st.crosswalk, 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection') that marks the entrance (st.entrance_of) of a carrier (st.travel_region) entering the intersection ego occupies (st.lane_enters), every crossing of its approaches, tied by relation atoms, never by distance; 'other traffic' is DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic other than ego, 'using the intersection' its footprint overlapping the intersection (st.intersection). 'lawfully' is not read (narrowing)."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"a8","why":"An advisory to drivers turning with the arrow about the signal opposing traffic faces: it imposes no duty and states no condition of this one, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"]}],"applicability":"ego is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and not a pedestrian (ru.pedestrian). At the judged observation ego occupies an intersection I, has occupied it at every observation since its last entry into it, and at that entry (the rise of ego's occupancy of I, read through a since operator) ego occupied a carrier c of kind st.travel_region entering I (st.lane_enters(c, I)) governed by a traffic signal d (dev.governs of c or I) displaying circular_red together with green_arrow(left), green_arrow(right) or green_arrow(u_turn).","obligation":"For the intersection I selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): ego is at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance), or both: for every road user p other than ego that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian) and occupies a crosswalk w marking the entrance of a carrier e that enters I (st.entrance_of(w, e), st.lane_enters(e, I)), it is not the case that their centres approach within p.conflict_horizon (prim.closest_approach_within) with a centre distance at that closest approach below p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance (prim.closest_approach_distance); and for every road user u other than ego that is traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) and occupies I, the same with p.conflict_clearance. With no such road user in the scene the duty is met.","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_clearance","p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","p.rest_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"a7","why":"The danger of a crash the right-of-way presupposes is read as a projected close approach of the centres under constant velocities; 'lawfully' is not read, so the yield is owed to every pedestrian within an adjacent crosswalk and every member of traffic within the intersection (the lawfulness of their presence refers to rules not in the library).","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, enters intersection I under circular_red with green_arrow(left) and turns left while a pedestrian walks in the crosswalk across the road it turns into (marking that road's approach carrier into I); ego keeps moving and their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the pedestrian clearance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but ego halts within I until the pedestrian has crossed, then completes the turn with no projected approach below the clearance."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego enters I while the signal governing its lane displays circular_green."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not record which carriers' entrances the crosswalks mark, so whether the pedestrian's crosswalk is one of I's is unknown.","masked":["st.entrance_of"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego turns left through I under the arrow with no pedestrian and no other road user in the scene: the duty binds ego alone and is met."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego turns left on the arrow while a car that entered I earlier is still crossing it; ego keeps moving and their projected closest approach falls within the horizon below the vehicle clearance."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"Time-to-collision horizon of the traffic-conflict technique: a projected approach of the centres within this time counts toward the danger of a crash.","source":"traffic-conflict technique; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the bodies of two passenger vehicles would touch or nearly touch (about a half-length plus a half-width of a design passenger car).","source":"design passenger car dimensions; proposed by NRS_484B_113_3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.pedestrian_conflict_clearance","unit":"m","value":2.5,"convention":"Centre-to-centre distance at the projected closest approach below which the body of a passenger vehicle and a pedestrian would touch or nearly touch: about a design passenger car's half-length plus a pedestrian's body radius.","source":"design passenger car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P) and pedestrian body ellipse (HCM)"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_413_2","law_refs":["NRS-484B-413-2"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"t1","text":"A signal of intention to turn right or left, or otherwise turn a vehicle from a direct course, shall be given continuously during","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t4","text":"not less than the last 100 feet traveled","role":"condition"},{"id":"t5","text":"in a business or residential district","role":"condition"},{"id":"t6","text":"and not less than the last 300 feet traveled","role":"condition"},{"id":"t7","text":"in any other area","role":"condition"},{"id":"t8","text":"prior to changing the course of a vehicle.","role":"trigger"},{"id":"t9","text":"This rule shall be observed, regardless of the weather.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"t1","atoms":["sig.turn_indicator","sig.hand_signal","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"A signal 'of intention' is the signal itself: sig.turn_indicator, 'the turn indicator state ∈ {off, left, right}', or sig.hand_signal, 'a driver's or rider's arm signal; meaning ∈ {no_signal, left, right, stop_or_slow, re_enter}', on the side of the turn ('to turn right or left, or otherwise turn ... from a direct course'), the turn itself being read by t8's concepts. 'given continuously during' is that matching signal at every observation of the window (holdsFor): an observation with the indicator off and no matching arm signal breaks it. 'Not a stand-in for: the turn or lane change itself' is respected: the signal is judged separately from the turn. 'a vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', except 'Devices moved by human power', 'Electric bicycles', electric personal assistive mobility devices and 'An electric scooter'), claimed whole."},{"span":"t4","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last 100 feet traveled' is a window measured in the distance ego travelled behind the onset (a .path window), read through kin.path_length, 'distance travelled along the body's path since the start of the trace, monotone'; the figure is the law's literal. It selects the window where t5 holds."},{"span":"t6","atoms":["kin.path_length"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last 300 feet traveled' is the same .path window with the law's other literal, through kin.path_length; it selects the window where t7 holds."},{"span":"t8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset","drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset","drv.motion.turning_left","drv.motion.turning_right"],"justification":"'changing the course of a vehicle' is a change of its heading to one side from an observed onset: drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset or drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset, each recognizing a continuous turning stretch whose heading change reaches the turn angle. 'prior to' places the window before the observed onset: the observation at which drv.motion.turning_left (or drv.motion.turning_right) last became true before the recognition, as those concepts' act records declare it. 'a vehicle' is DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"t5","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."},{"span":"t7","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"t9","why":"The duty holds in every weather: no condition of the weather restricts it, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle). The judged observation is the recognition of a left turn from an observed onset (drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset with p.left_turn_min_angle, p.turn_yaw_tolerance, p.rest_speed_tolerance, p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph) or of a right turn from an observed onset (drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset with p.right_turn_min_angle and the same tolerances).","obligation":"Event, recognition and history (rule 4d): the event is the change of course; it is recognized at the judged observation; its observed onset is the last observation at which drv.motion.turning_left (for a left turn; drv.motion.turning_right for a right turn, each with p.turn_yaw_tolerance and p.rest_speed_tolerance) became true, the turning state having held at every observation since (a since operator: turning since (rise of turning and W)). W, read at that onset: where asm.business_or_residence_district holds there, at every observation of the window of the literal 100 ft of path travelled by ego behind the onset (holdsFor .path, kin.path_length), ego's turn indicator is left (sig.turn_indicator = left) or its arm signal means left (sig.hand_signal = left); where it does not hold, the same over the window of the literal 300 ft. For a right turn the matching side is right. The window ends at the onset and is the words' own bound; a window that reaches past the start of the recording is unknown (windowTruncated), as is the duty where the assumption is undeclared and the two windows decide differently. Conduct after the onset is not read.","params":["p.left_turn_min_angle","p.right_turn_min_angle","p.turn_yaw_tolerance","p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph"],"narrowings":[{"span":"t1","why":"A change of course is read as a turn whose heading change from its observed onset reaches the turn angle; a lane change or a gentle departure from the course, whose heading change stays below it, is not read, and a road bend followed through that angle in one turning stretch is read as a turn.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, with the business-or-residence-district assumption declared, drives along a straight roadway and turns left at an intersection; its left indicator lights only over the final few metres before the turn begins, so at the onset the window of the last 100 ft holds observations with the indicator off and no arm signal."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"as in forbid, but the left indicator is lit at every observation over well more than the last 100 ft travelled before the turn's onset."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego drives straight along a straight roadway and makes no turn."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source does not observe turn indicators and observes no arm signal, so whether a signal was given is unknown.","masked":["sig.turn_indicator"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego turns right with the assumption declared false (any other area); its right indicator is lit over the last 100 ft before the onset but not over the last 300 ft."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego, the assumption declared, turns left with its indicator off but its arm signal meaning left at every observation over the last 100 ft before the onset."}],"literals":[{"span":"t4","text":"100 feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"t6","text":"300 feet","value":300,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.left_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a turn: a leftward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.right_turn_min_angle","unit":"deg","value":60.0,"convention":"Lower bound of a right turn: a rightward heading change below it is a drift or lane change, not a turn onto another way.","source":"junction turning geometry, mirrored from the left-turn band"},{"name":"p.turn_yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","value":5.0,"convention":"Yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none: above lane-keeping yaw noise, below the yaw rates of turning at a junction.","source":"vehicle yaw-rate noise and junction turning rates; proposed by NRS_484B_227_1_o3 this iteration"},{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"NRS_484B_440_1_o1","law_refs":["NRS-484B-440-1"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"Upon any highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e2","text":"outside of a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"no person shall stop, park or leave standing","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e4","text":"any vehicle,","role":"subject"},{"id":"e5","text":"whether attended or unattended,","role":"condition"},{"id":"e6","text":"upon the paved or main-traveled part of the highway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e7","text":"when it is practicable to stop, park or so leave such vehicle off such part of the highway,","role":"standard"},{"id":"e8","text":"but in every event","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e9","text":"an unobstructed width of the highway opposite a standing vehicle shall be left","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e10","text":"for the free passage of other vehicles","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e11","text":"and a clear view of such stopped vehicles shall be available from a distance of 200 feet in each direction upon such highway.","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"This section shall not apply to the driver of any vehicle which is disabled while on the paved or main-traveled portion of a highway in such manner and to such extent that it is impossible to avoid stopping and temporarily leaving such disabled vehicle in such position.","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway is 'the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders', carrying DEF-NRS-484A-095 ('the entire width between the boundary lines of every way dedicated to a public authority'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies). 'Not a stand-in for: the roadway' is respected: the part of it the duty reads is e6."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap","dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.human_direction","dev.governs"],"derived":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"'stop' where prohibited is DEF-NRS-484A-260, 'any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the directions of a police officer or official traffic-control device'; 'park' (DEF-NRS-484A-155) and 'standing' (DEF-NRS-484A-250) are halts too, so their union is a halt (drv.motion.at_rest) other than the excepted ones, which the rule carries beside it: a halt behind a road user ahead in ego's lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) that is itself at rest within p.queue_gap (rel.surface_gap), or a halt while a stop indication governs ego's carrier (dev.governs of a dev.traffic_signal displaying circular_red or a red_arrow, a dev.stop_sign, or a dev.human_direction indicating stop). 'no person shall' is read through the vehicle's halt (observable_reading agency)."},{"span":"e4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle ('every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', with its exceptions), claimed whole."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.roadway","st.shoulder","st.on_way"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the paved or main-traveled part of the highway': the main-traveled part is the roadway (st.roadway, 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder'), the paved part also a shoulder whose paved attribute holds (st.shoulder, 'paved attribute'); ego's footprint overlaps one (rel.occupies) lying on the highway of e1 (st.on_way)."},{"span":"e13","atoms":["sig.hazard","kin.engine_running"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on e13): that a vehicle is disabled so that it cannot avoid stopping is a condition of the vehicle no atom carries; hazard lamps (sig.hazard, 'both indicators flashing together') are a lamp state, and an engine stopped (kin.engine_running) is 'Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt' nor for a vehicle that cannot move."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e7","standard":"practicable","concepts":["drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.shoulder","st.parking_space","rel.occupies"],"params":["p.offroad_stop_reach"],"convention":"Off-road standing place within braking reach: halting off the paved or main-traveled part is practicable where a region off it lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of the halted vehicle's body (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry): a shoulder whose paved attribute does not hold (st.shoulder) or a parking space (st.parking_space) that does not overlap the roadway. The distance to the nearest such place enters the bound.","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"The map or the trace declares the territory at the road user's position a business district or a residence district."}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"e5","why":"Whether the vehicle is attended or unattended does not change the duty: it is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a vehicle; at the judged observation ego occupies a roadway, or a shoulder whose paved attribute holds, lying on a highway (st.on_way), asm.business_or_residence_district does not hold there, and ego is halted (drv.motion.at_rest with p.rest_speed_tolerance) other than behind a road user ahead in its lane at rest within p.queue_gap or under a stop indication governing its carrier. Exception: a disabled vehicle (gap on e13).","obligation":"It is not the case that a region off the paved or main-traveled part (a shoulder whose paved attribute does not hold, or a parking space not overlapping the roadway) lies within p.offroad_stop_reach of ego's body (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry).","params":["p.rest_speed_tolerance","p.queue_gap","p.offroad_stop_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e3","why":"'no person shall' is read through the vehicle's halt, whoever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e7","why":"Practicability is read only through an off-road standing place within reach; its size and surface are not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway of a rural highway, the assumption declared false, with an unpaved shoulder beside it within the reach and no road user ahead."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway of a rural highway where no unpaved shoulder or parking space lies within the reach."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego halts in the roadway with the business-or-residence-district assumption declared true."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in forbid, but the source maps regions without outlines, so the distance to the shoulder is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.rest_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"Stop-detection noise floor: the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement, set at the resolution of the speed measurement so that a complete cessation from movement is recognized despite sensor jitter.","source":"speed-sensor resolution; proposed by LVMC_11_30_030 this iteration"},{"name":"p.queue_gap","unit":"m","value":10.0,"convention":"Gap to a halted road user ahead in the lane within which a halt counts as made to avoid conflict with it: a queued vehicle's standstill spacing plus a margin.","source":"queue standstill spacing (HCM)"},{"name":"p.offroad_stop_reach","unit":"m","value":30.0,"convention":"Distance within which an off-road standing place counts as practicable for a halting vehicle: the braking distance of a moderate approach, within which the driver can halt on it instead.","source":"stopping-distance model (AASHTO Green Book)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"e13","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.disabled` | a vehicle that cannot move under its own power (a breakdown, crash damage, a lost wheel or a flat tyre), as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** a halt, hazard lamps lit or an engine stopped | general","nearest":["sig.hazard: 'both indicators flashing together' (a lamp state, not whether the vehicle can move)","kin.engine_running: 'Not a stand-in for: motion or a halt' (a stopped engine is no disablement, and a disabled vehicle may run its engine)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
