{"node_id":"NRS_484B_600_1a","law_refs":["NRS-484B-600-1a"],"subject":{"binder":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"u1","text":"It is unlawful for any person to drive or operate","role":"subject"},{"id":"u2","text":"a vehicle of any kind or character","role":"subject"},{"id":"u3","text":"at: A rate of speed","role":"obligation"},{"id":"u4","text":"greater than is reasonable or proper, having due regard for the traffic, surface and width of the highway, the weather and other highway conditions.","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"u1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'to drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (observable_reading agency): its speed (kin.speed, 'magnitude of velocity'), whoever or whatever controls it."},{"span":"u2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle: 'every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway', except 'Devices moved by human power or used exclusively upon stationary rails', 'Electric bicycles', electric personal assistive mobility devices and 'An electric scooter'; claimed whole. 'of any kind or character' adds no restriction."},{"span":"u3","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'A rate of speed' is kin.speed, 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s; kin.accel_longitudinal's 'Not a stand-in for: speed' confirms speed is read directly."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"u4","standard":"a rate of speed greater than is reasonable or proper, having due regard for the traffic, surface and width of the highway, the weather and other highway conditions","concepts":["drv.motion.stopping_distance","kin.speed","st.sight_distance","env.visibility","env.wet_road","env.ice_or_snow","env.precipitation","st.curvature","st.lane","st.lane_width","rel.occupies","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.perception_reaction_time","p.stopping_decel_dry","p.stopping_decel_wet","p.stopping_decel_ice","p.curve_lateral_accel","p.lane_width_speed_time"],"convention":"Stopping-sight-distance model of highway design (AASHTO Green Book), with the curve side-friction and lane-width relations of the same guides. Surface and weather select the deceleration: p.stopping_decel_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.stopping_decel_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.stopping_decel_dry (Term.cond over drv.motion.stopping_distance calls with p.perception_reaction_time). The stopping distance may not exceed the sight distance of the place (st.sight_distance) nor the visibility distance (env.visibility); for every road user ahead of ego in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane), the traffic, the gap (rel.surface_gap) may not fall below the speed times p.perception_reaction_time; the speed squared times the curvature (st.curvature) may not exceed p.curve_lateral_accel; the speed times p.lane_width_speed_time may not exceed the width (st.lane_width) of the lane ego occupies (st.lane, rel.occupies). Each measured magnitude enters its bound. The standard is the whole duty: the rule is a surrogate.","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"ego is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle); the duty is judged at every observation.","obligation":"At every observation, with D the stopping distance of ego (drv.motion.stopping_distance with p.perception_reaction_time and the deceleration selected by Term.cond: p.stopping_decel_ice where env.ice_or_snow holds, else p.stopping_decel_wet where env.wet_road or env.precipitation holds, else p.stopping_decel_dry): D is at or below st.sight_distance at ego's place and at or below env.visibility; ego's speed (kin.speed) squared times st.curvature at its place is at or below p.curve_lateral_accel; for every lane l ego occupies (rel.occupies), ego's speed times p.lane_width_speed_time is at or below st.lane_width of l; and for every road user u other than ego that is ahead of ego in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane), the gap between them (rel.surface_gap) is at or above ego's speed times p.perception_reaction_time. With no such road user the last clause is met.","params":["p.perception_reaction_time","p.stopping_decel_dry","p.stopping_decel_wet","p.stopping_decel_ice","p.curve_lateral_accel","p.lane_width_speed_time"],"narrowings":[{"span":"u1","why":"'drive or operate' is read through the vehicle's motion, whoever or whatever controls it.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"u4","why":"The factors are read only through the contracts named: traffic through the road users ahead in ego's lane (crossing and oncoming traffic, and its density, are not read); surface through wet and icy or snow-covered states; width through the width of the lane ego occupies; weather through precipitation and visibility distance; the catch-all 'other highway conditions' only through curvature and the sight distance of the place (grade, darkness and works are not read).","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego, a passenger car, drives at highway speed on a dry straight road in dense fog: its stopping distance far exceeds the visibility distance."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego drives at a moderate speed on a dry, straight, wide road in clear weather with a long sight distance and no road user close ahead."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego is a bicycle (ru.bicycle), a device moved by human power that the vehicle aggregate does not include."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in permit, but the source does not supply sight distances, so whether the stopping distance fits within the sight distance is unknown.","masked":["st.sight_distance"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego drives on an icy road at a speed whose dry stopping distance fits within the sight distance but whose icy stopping distance does not."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego takes a sharp bend at a speed whose lateral acceleration exceeds the side-friction limit, on a dry road with ample sight distance and no other road user."},{"name":"branch_3","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego drives alone on the road at a moderate speed in clear weather: no road user is ahead and every bound holds."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.perception_reaction_time","unit":"s","value":2.5,"convention":"Brake reaction time of the stopping-sight-distance model: the time from the appearance of a hazard to the application of the brakes.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, stopping sight distance"},{"name":"p.stopping_decel_dry","unit":"m/s^2","value":4.5,"convention":"Deceleration a driver attains in a controlled stop on a dry paved surface.","source":"AASHTO Green Book and braking studies (Fambro et al., NCHRP 400)"},{"name":"p.stopping_decel_wet","unit":"m/s^2","value":3.4,"convention":"Deceleration of the stopping-sight-distance model, which most drivers attain on a wet pavement.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, stopping sight distance"},{"name":"p.stopping_decel_ice","unit":"m/s^2","value":1.5,"convention":"Deceleration attainable on an icy or snow-covered surface, from the low friction coefficient of such surfaces.","source":"winter road friction measurements (PIARC)"},{"name":"p.curve_lateral_accel","unit":"m/s^2","value":2.0,"convention":"Side-friction limit of horizontal curve design: the lateral acceleration a curve may impose on a vehicle at a comfortable, safe speed.","source":"AASHTO Green Book, horizontal curve side friction factors"},{"name":"p.lane_width_speed_time","unit":"s","value":0.16,"convention":"Lane width per unit of speed from the lane-width and design-speed relation of highway design guides (a full-width lane for a high design speed): the speed times it may not exceed the lane's width.","source":"AASHTO Green Book lane widths by design speed"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry","kind":"quantity","contract":"The heading change of road user a since it entered region r: the signed change of the direction its body points (degrees, left positive), accumulated from the observation at which a's footprint last came to overlap r, where it is zero, to the observation, whether or not a still overlaps r. Measured by integrating a's yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) from the observation at which a's occupancy of r (rel.occupies) last became true, with the step bound, the largest interval between consecutive observations integrated across. It is unknown where that entry is not observed (a occupied r from the start of the recording, or an unknown occupancy could hide the entry), where an interval between consecutive observations since the observation before the entry exceeds the step bound, or where a yaw rate since the entry is missing. Not a stand-in for a turn: it is a magnitude that a caller bounds, and a road user that follows a bend of the way through r accumulates the bend's heading change.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"},{"name":"r","sort":"region"}],"params":[{"name":"step","unit":"ms","meaning":"the step bound: the largest interval between consecutive observations the integration crosses"}],"elements":[{"span":"the observation at which a's occupancy of r (rel.occupies) last became true","atoms":["rel.occupies"],"concepts":[],"justification":"rel.occupies is 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; its rise marks the entry from which the heading change is counted."},{"span":"integrating a's yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive)","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.yaw_rate is the 'rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left'; its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature' is stated in the contract: the concept counts the road user's own heading change, bend or turn alike."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a enters r heading along one axis, turns left a quarter turn inside r and leaves it; the instance bounds the value to a left band and the value read at the exit lies within it."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a crosses r without turning; the value read at the exit stays near zero, outside the instance's left band."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"as in holds, but the source supplies no yaw rate, so the heading change is unknown.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_307_9a_o1","NRS_484B_307_9b_o1","NRS_484B_307_9b_o2","NRS_484B_307_9b_o3","NRS_484B_307_9b_o4"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.turning_right","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a is turning to the right at an observation: it moves and its heading turns to the right. Measured as a not at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with the speed tolerance does not hold) and its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) at or below the negative of the yaw tolerance, the rate below which a change of heading counts as none. A state at each observation while a turn is under way, not a completed manoeuvre: it does not say how far the turn goes, and it holds alike where the road user follows a bend of the road to the right. Not a stand-in for the turn indicator or for a declared intention to turn.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","meaning":"the yaw rate magnitude below which a change of heading counts as none"},{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which the road user counts as at rest"}],"elements":[{"span":"a not at rest (drv.motion.at_rest with the speed tolerance does not hold)","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.at_rest"],"justification":"drv.motion.at_rest holds at each observation at which the speed is at or below the speed tolerance; its negation is the road user moving."},{"span":"its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) at or below the negative of the yaw tolerance","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.yaw_rate is 'positive when the heading turns to the left', so a rightward turn is a yaw rate below the negative tolerance; 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature' is stated: a bend followed to the right is included."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a moves through a junction with a yaw rate well below the negative of the tolerance."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a moves along a straight road with a yaw rate near zero."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"a moves, but the source supplies no yaw rate.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null,"differs_from":{"concept":"drv.motion.turning_left","why":"the opposite hand: the yaw rate at or below the negative of the tolerance rather than at or above it"}}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a turns to the left from an observed onset: over one continuous stretch in which it moves and its heading turns to the left, its heading changes to the left by at least the turn angle, the heading change below which turning counts as no change of course. Measured as drv.motion.turning_left (with the yaw tolerance and the speed tolerance) holding at every observation since the observation at which it last became true, and the heading change since that observation (integrated from kin.yaw_rate, degrees, left positive, with the step bound, the largest interval between consecutive observations integrated across) at or above the turn angle. The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_left last became true. The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change since that beginning first reaches the turn angle. The concept holds at the recognition observation only. Conduct before the observed beginning is no part of the act, and where that beginning is not observed (the stretch began before the recording, or an unknown turning state could hide its start) whether the act occurred is unknown. A stretch that ends before its heading change reaches the turn angle is no turn; a road user that follows a bend of the way through that angle turns in this sense. Not a stand-in for the turn indicator or a declared intention to turn, nor for a lane change, whose heading change stays below the turn angle.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"turn_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the heading change below which turning counts as no change of course"},{"name":"yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","meaning":"the yaw rate below which a change of heading counts as none"},{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which the road user counts as at rest"},{"name":"step","unit":"ms","meaning":"the step bound of the heading integration"}],"act":{"boundary":"event","onset":"The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_left last became true.","recognition":"The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change since that beginning first reaches the turn angle.","extent":"The concept holds at the recognition observation only.","history":"Conduct before the observed beginning is no part of the act, and where that beginning is not observed (the stretch began before the recording, or an unknown turning state could hide its start) whether the act occurred is unknown."},"elements":[{"span":"drv.motion.turning_left (with the yaw tolerance and the speed tolerance) holding at every observation since the observation at which it last became true","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.turning_left"],"justification":"drv.motion.turning_left is the state 'it moves and its heading turns to the left' at each observation; its last rise is the onset and its holding since is the continuous stretch."},{"span":"the heading change since that observation (integrated from kin.yaw_rate, degrees, left positive, with the step bound","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.yaw_rate, 'positive when the heading turns to the left', integrated since the onset (Term.headingSince with the step bound) is the heading change of the act; 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature' is stated in the contract."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a, moving, starts yawing left at a junction and keeps yawing until its heading has turned a quarter turn; at the observation where the heading change first reaches the turn angle the concept holds."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a drifts left for a lane change; its yaw stops long before the heading change reaches the turn angle."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"a turns at a junction, but the source supplies no yaw rate.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset","kind":"formula","contract":"Road user a turns to the right from an observed onset: over one continuous stretch in which it moves and its heading turns to the right, its heading changes to the right by at least the turn angle, the heading change below which turning counts as no change of course. Measured as drv.motion.turning_right (with the yaw tolerance and the speed tolerance) holding at every observation since the observation at which it last became true, and the heading change since that observation (integrated from kin.yaw_rate, degrees, left positive, with the step bound, the largest interval between consecutive observations integrated across) at or below the negative of the turn angle. The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_right last became true. The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change since that beginning first reaches the negative of the turn angle. The concept holds at the recognition observation only. Conduct before the observed beginning is no part of the act, and where that beginning is not observed (the stretch began before the recording, or an unknown turning state could hide its start) whether the act occurred is unknown. A stretch that ends before its heading change reaches the negative of the turn angle is no turn; a road user that follows a bend of the way through that angle turns in this sense. Not a stand-in for the turn indicator or a declared intention to turn, nor for a lane change, whose heading change stays short of the turn angle.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"turn_angle","unit":"deg","meaning":"the heading change below which turning counts as no change of course"},{"name":"yaw_tolerance","unit":"deg/s","meaning":"the yaw rate magnitude below which a change of heading counts as none"},{"name":"speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which the road user counts as at rest"},{"name":"step","unit":"ms","meaning":"the step bound of the heading integration"}],"act":{"boundary":"event","onset":"The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_right last became true.","recognition":"The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change since that beginning first reaches the negative of the turn angle.","extent":"The concept holds at the recognition observation only.","history":"Conduct before the observed beginning is no part of the act, and where that beginning is not observed (the stretch began before the recording, or an unknown turning state could hide its start) whether the act occurred is unknown."},"elements":[{"span":"drv.motion.turning_right (with the yaw tolerance and the speed tolerance) holding at every observation since the observation at which it last became true","atoms":[],"concepts":["drv.motion.turning_right"],"justification":"drv.motion.turning_right is the state 'it moves and its heading turns to the right' at each observation; its last rise is the onset and its holding since is the continuous stretch."},{"span":"the heading change since that observation (integrated from kin.yaw_rate, degrees, left positive, with the step bound","atoms":["kin.yaw_rate"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.yaw_rate, 'positive when the heading turns to the left', integrated since the onset (Term.headingSince with the step bound): a right turn is a negative heading change; 'Not a stand-in for: road curvature' is stated in the contract."}],"residues":[],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a, moving, starts yawing right at a junction and keeps yawing until its heading has turned a quarter turn to the right; the concept holds where the change first reaches the negative of the turn angle."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a drifts right for a lane change; its yaw stops long before the heading change reaches the turn angle."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"a turns at a junction, but the source supplies no yaw rate.","masked":["kin.yaw_rate"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_413_2"],"supersedes":null,"differs_from":{"concept":"drv.motion.left_turn_from_onset","why":"the opposite hand: a rightward stretch and a negative heading change"}}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.stopping_distance","kind":"quantity","contract":"The distance road user a would travel before coming to rest if it began to brake after a reaction time, at the observation: its speed (kin.speed, m/s) times the reaction time, plus the square of its speed divided by twice the deceleration (m). Computed from the current speed only, under a constant deceleration on a level road. Not a stand-in for a sight distance or a gap to another road user, which a caller compares it with, nor for a braking manoeuvre actually made.","definition":null,"args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"reaction_time","unit":"s","meaning":"the time from the appearance of a hazard to the application of the brakes"},{"name":"deceleration","unit":"m/s^2","meaning":"the constant deceleration of the braking"}],"elements":[{"span":"its speed (kin.speed, m/s)","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed is the 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s; the distance is computed from it alone, with the caller's reaction time and deceleration."}],"residues":[],"literals":[{"value":2,"unit":"count","why":"the factor of the braking distance: the square of the speed divided by twice the deceleration"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"a moves at a moderate speed; the instance bounds include the value computed from its speed, the reaction time and the deceleration."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"a moves at a high speed; the value exceeds the instance's upper bound."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"the source does not supply a's speed.","masked":["kin.speed"]}],"used_by":["NRS_484B_600_1a"],"supersedes":null}

