pies","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk is the 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', which carries DEF-NRS-484A-240 ('that portion of a highway between the curb lines or the lateral lines of a highway and the adjacent property lines intended for the use of pedestrians'); ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies) is its walking on it, read at the earlier observation at which ego met the obstruction. 'Not a stand-in for: a crosswalk' does not apply."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"st.obstruction is 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user'; 'encounters' is ego at the obstruction while on the sidewalk: drv.position.near_region(ego, o) with p.obstruction_reach, over the body-to-region distance of st.region_geometry, the anchor of the obstruction to ego. 'to his or her mobility' is read through ego's conduct at it (s8)."},{"span":"s4","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only, to show the shortfall (gap on s4): a missing section of sidewalk is no 'physical object' (st.obstruction), and the absence of a sidewalk region (st.sidewalk) is not a stretch a source records that a pedestrian meets."},{"span":"s5","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'may proceed' is ego's travel off the sidewalk: its footprint overlaps (rel.occupies) a region of kind st.travel_region ('a lane ..., a bicycle lane or path, a roadway ..., a shoulder, or an intersection'), which excludes 'a sidewalk'."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway","st.on_way","st.travel_region","st.sidewalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the immediately adjacent highway' is the same way as the sidewalk: the travel region ego occupies and the sidewalk both lie on one highway region (st.on_way; st.highway 'including sidewalks and shoulders'); belonging is read through st.on_way, never a distance ('Not a stand-in for: nearness to a way')."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.sidewalk","st.obstruction"],"derived":["drv.position.near_region"],"justification":"A purpose read through the conduct it explains (observable_reading purpose): since the last observation at which ego occupied the sidewalk while at that obstruction, ego has occupied no sidewalk."},{"span":"s9","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'Such a pedestrian' is the pedestrian of s1 proceeding under the first sentence: the same binder and aggregate."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["st.sidewalk","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"'as far to the side of the highway near the sidewalk' is ego's position across the way relative to the sidewalk: the ground distance from ego's body outline to the sidewalk region (st.region_geometry, 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'), the sidewalk being the one ego left (s2, re-bound). Its exclusion 'Not a stand-in for: occupancy' does not apply: ego is off the sidewalk."},{"span":"s13","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.bicycle_lane_or_path"],"derived":[],"justification":"'a lane provided for bicycles, electric bicycles or electric scooters' is st.bicycle_lane_or_path, 'lane or separate path reserved for bicycles and the devices a jurisdiction groups with them'; ego's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies). The class words qualify the lane, not a road user the duty reads, so no aggregate is claimed."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s11","standard":"as possible","concepts":["st.region_geometry","prim.region_lateral_offset","st.obstruction"],"params":["p.pedestrian_edge_margin"],"convention":"Lateral position at the edge: the body-to-sidewalk distance (st.region_geometry) is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin, a step's width plus the shy distance a walker keeps from a curb; where an obstruction lies across ego's side toward the sidewalk (prim.region_lateral_offset of the obstruction of the same sign as the sidewalk's and of smaller magnitude), the nearest thing ego can keep to is that obstruction, and its body-to-obstruction distance is held to the same margin. The obstruction's own lateral reach moves the bound.","surrogate":false},{"span":"s14","standard":"impassable","concepts":["prim.region_lateral_offset","st.obstruction","drv.position.near_region","st.region_geometry","st.sidewalk"],"params":["p.obstruction_reach"],"convention":"An area is impassable on foot where a physical object blocks it: an obstruction lies laterally between ego and the sidewalk (prim.region_lateral_offset of the obstruction of the same sign as the sidewalk's and of smaller magnitude) and within p.obstruction_reach of ego (drv.position.near_region over st.region_geometry).","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s12","why":"A permission to walk in either direction on the highway: the duty to keep to the side near the sidewalk is the same in either direction, so the duty is the same whether or not its words hold.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"ego","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"]}],"applicability":"As NRS_484B_297_6_o1: ego is a pedestrian; at the judged observation ego occupies no sidewalk and occupies a travel region lying on a highway h on which a sidewalk s also lies, and since the last observation at which ego occupied s while at an obstruction (drv.position.near_region with p.obstruction_reach), ego has occupied no sidewalk. Exception (c): not where ego occupies a bicycle lane or path (st.bicycle_lane_or_path) and an obstruction lies laterally between ego and s within p.obstruction_reach of ego.","obligation":"For the sidewalk s selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the same relations): the distance from ego's body to s (st.region_geometry) is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin, or an obstruction o lies laterally between ego and s (prim.region_lateral_offset of o of the same sign as that of s and of smaller magnitude) and the distance from ego's body to o is at or below p.pedestrian_edge_margin.","params":["p.pedestrian_edge_margin","p.obstruction_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s8","why":"The purpose of moving around the obstruction is read through the conduct it explains: the pedestrian left the sidewalk at the obstruction and has not yet returned.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"},{"span":"s14","why":"'impassable' is read only through a physical object between the bicycle lane and the sidewalk; a strip impassable for other reasons (standing vehicles, a drop-off) is not read.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks down the middle of the adjacent lane, well beyond the edge margin from both the sidewalk and the barrier."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"ego leaves the sidewalk at a barrier and walks along the roadway hugging the barrier's outer side, within the edge margin of it, then of the sidewalk."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego stays on the sidewalk throughout."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"ego walks in the roadway after leaving the sidewalk at a barrier, but the source maps regions without outlines, so ego's distance to the sidewalk and to the barrier is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"ego walks in a bicycle lane beside a strip of excavation that lies between the lane and the sidewalk within the reach: exception (c) applies."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.pedestrian_edge_margin","unit":"m","value":1.0,"convention":"Lateral body-to-edge distance within which a pedestrian walking on the highway counts as at the side next to the sidewalk or the obstruction: a step's width plus the shy distance a walker keeps from a curb or an object.","source":"pedestrian shy distance (HCM pedestrian facilities)"},{"name":"p.obstruction_reach","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"Reach within which a pedestrian counts as at an obstruction: a walking pedestrian's body width plus one step.","source":"pedestrian body ellipse and walking step length (HCM pedestrian space)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"s4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_interruption` | a stretch along a sidewalk where no walkable sidewalk exists (a section missing, removed, closed or broken up), carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so a pedestrian's arrival at it is read through st.region_geometry **Not a stand-in for:** an object standing on the sidewalk (st.obstruction) | general","nearest":["st.obstruction: 'a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user' (a missing section of sidewalk is no object, so the atom leaves out where the duty arises)","st.sidewalk: 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (the absence of a sidewalk region is not a stretch the source records that a pedestrian meets)"]}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
